"VE NEVER BEEN SO HUMIL-IATED IN ALL MY LIFE."

241
00:14:32,684 --> 00:14:33,684
THAT WAS THE MEANEST...

242
00:14:35,687 --> 00:14:38,524
HOW COULD YOU MAKE FUN OF MEIN PUBLIC?

243
00:14:38,857 --> 00:14:39,834
DIANA...

244
00:14:39,858 --> 00:14:41,527
| WASN'T MAKING FUN.

245
00:14:41,860 --> 00:14:42,860
| WAS JUST TEASING.

246
00:14:44,696 --> 00:14:45,696
/M SORRY.

247
00:14:45,864 --> 00:14:47,624
YOU ALWAYS HAVE TO BE THE CENTRE OF ATTENTION

248
00:14:47,866 --> 00:14:50,411
WHENEVER GILBERT BLYTHE IS IN ANYONE'S COMPANY.

249
00:14:50,744 --> 00:14:51,744
THAT'S NOT TRUE.

250
00:14:55,707 --> 00:14:58,252
PLEASE FORGIVE ME, DIANA.

251
00:14:58,710 --> 00:14:59,990
| DIDN'T MEAN TO PICK A QUARREL.

252
00:15:00,379 --> 00:15:01,713
[ Sigh ]

253
00:15:02,256 --> 00:15:04,633
WHY COULDN'T YOU HAVE TOLD ME ABOUT YOU AND FRED YOURSELF?

254
00:15:04,967 --> 00:15:10,472
[ Sob/sniffle | | FEEL LIKE I'VE LOST MY BEST FRIEND.

255
00:15:10,806 --> 00:15:12,641
YOU WERE... YOU WERE SO BUSY,

256
00:15:12,975 --> 00:15:16,645
WRITING YOUX BOOK AND MARKING EXAM PAPERS.

257
00:15:16,979 --> 00:15:18,647
IT JUST HAPPENED.

258
00:15:18,981 --> 00:15:19,958
[ Sniffling |.

259
00:15:19,982 --> 00:15:22,484
AND HE ASKED ME...

260
00:15:22,818 --> 00:15:24,653
[ Laugh |]

261
00:15:24,987 --> 00:15:26,321
I'M REALLY HAPPY.

262
00:15:27,823 --> 00:15:30,659
BUT IT DOES SEEM RIDICULOUS

263
00:15:30,993 --> 00:15:34,663
TO THINK OF ME BEING ENGAGED TO FRED, DOESN'T IT?

264
00:15:34,997 --> 00:15:37,666
OH, | DON'T CARE WHAT HE LOOKS LIKE.

265
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,668
HE... HE'S GOT A GOOD HEART.

266
00:15:40,002 --> 00:15:41,753
HE'S SO THOUGHTFUL.

267
00:15:42,087 --> 00:15:45,424
WE'LL PROBABLY MAKE A PUDGY OLD COUPLE SOME DAY,

268
00:15:45,841 --> 00:15:46,841
BUT IT DOESN'T MATTER.

269
00:15:50,679 --> 00:15:52,431
| AM GLAD FOR YOU, DIANA.

270
00:15:52,723 --> 00:15:55,350
DON'T YOU EVER MEAN TO GET MARRIED?

271
00:15:55,642 --> 00:15:57,603
PERHAPS, IF | MEET THE RIGHT ONE.

272
00:15:59,605 --> 00:16:01,440
WHAT ABOUT GILBERT?

273
00:16:01,899 --> 00:16:04,234
GILBERT'S JUST A CHUM.

274
00:16:04,568 --> 00:16:06,069
| DON'T CARE FOR HIM IN THAT WAY.

275
00:16:06,403 --> 00:16:09,239
YOU KNOW WHAT MY IDEAL IS, DIANA.

276
00:16:09,573 --> 00:16:13,243
TALL, IRRESISTIBLY HANDSOME,

277
00:16:13,577 --> 00:16:15,496
PROUD AND MELANCHOLIC.

278
00:16:17,456 --> 00:16:21,251
BUT PEOPLE'S IDEALS CHANGE SOMETIMES.

279
00:16:21,585 --> 00:16:23,170
MINE WOULDN'T.

280
00:16:23,504 --> 00:16:26,006
| WOULDN'T CARE FOR ANY MAN WHO DIDN'T FULFIL THEM.

281
00:16:26,423 --> 00:16:27,549
WHAT IF YOU NEVER MEET HIM?

282
00:16:28,091 --> 00:16:30,260
WELL, THEN | SHALL DIE AN OLD MAID.

283
00:16:30,594 --> 00:16:34,264
OH, | SUPPOSE YOU'RE RIGHT TO BE DISCRIMINATING.

284
00:16:34,598 --> 00:16:36,576
HALF THE MEN ACROSS THE COUNTRY WILL BE COURTING YOU

285
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,268
WHEN YOUR STORY IS PUBLISHED.

286
00:16:38,602 --> 00:16:41,396
YOU'RE GOING TO BE FAMOUS, AND I'LL BE SO PUD.

287
00:16:43,774 --> 00:16:44,774
WHAT IS IT?

288
00:16:46,068 --> 00:16:47,694
OH...

289
00:16:49,780 --> 00:16:52,574
"WOMAN'S HOME JOURNAL" SENT IT BACK.

290
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:54,576
WHAT?

291
00:16:54,952 --> 00:16:56,578
WELL, THEIR EDITOR MUST BE CRAZY.

292
00:16:56,954 --> 00:16:58,580
WHAT REASON DID HE GIVE?

293
00:16:58,956 --> 00:17:00,666
NO REASON AT ALL, JUST A PRINTED SLIP

294
00:17:01,041 --> 00:17:02,376
SAYING IT WASN'T ACCEPTABLE.

295
00:17:02,876 --> 00:17:04,670
THAT'S RIDICULOUS! THEY MUSTN'T HAVE READ IT.

296
00:17:05,045 --> 00:17:07,673
I'M GOING TO CANCEL MY SUBSCRIPTION IMMEDIATELY.

297
00:17:08,048 --> 00:17:09,675
"AVERILS ATONEMENT~"

298
00:17:10,050 --> 00:17:14,680
IT SOUNDED SO INSPIRING AND ROMANTIC.

299
00:17:15,055 --> 00:17:16,682
BUT YOU CAN TELL ME TRUTHFULLY, DIANA,

300
00:17:17,057 --> 00:17:20,686
IF YOU RECALL ANY MAJOR FAULTS IN MY STORY.

301
00:17:21,895 --> 00:17:23,272
[ Sigh ] WELL...

302
00:17:25,148 --> 00:17:28,694
T-THE PART WHERE... WHERE AVERIL MAKES THE CAKE...

303
00:17:29,069 --> 00:17:33,699
DOESN'T... IT DOESN'T SEEM TO MATCH THE REST OF THE STORY.

304
00:17:34,074 --> 00:17:36,952
THAT'S ONE OF THE MOST ROMANTIC PARTS IN THE WHOLE STORY.

305
00:17:37,703 --> 00:17:39,903
IT'S A WELL-KNOWN FACT THAT GREAT LADIES OF OLD BELIEVED

306
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:42,708
THAT THE CULINARY ARTS ALSO FED THE SOUL.

307
00:17:43,083 --> 00:17:45,043
WELL, I'LL HAVE TO READ IT AGAIN

308
00:17:45,335 --> 00:17:47,713
TO REMEMBER WHAT MY FIRST OPINION WAS.

309
00:17:48,088 --> 00:17:51,717
IF YOU LET ME KEEP IT, MAYBE | CAN SUGGEST SOME CHANGES.

310
00:17:52,092 --> 00:17:55,721
YOU DON'T KNOW HOW DISCOURAGING ITISTOGETA REJECTION, DIANA.

311
00:17:56,096 --> 00:17:58,724
AND RIGHT WHEN MIN THE MIDST OF WRITING A NEW EPIC:

312
00:17:59,099 --> 00:18:00,809
"" ROSAMUND'S REVENGE.'

313
00:18:01,184 --> 00:18:03,812
THIS CERTAINLY TAKES THE BLOOM OFF THE ROSE.

314
00:18:04,187 --> 00:18:05,164
[awling of cow ]

315
00:18:05,188 --> 00:18:06,815
DON'T BE DISCOURAGED. ANNE SHIRLEY!

316
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:09,030
I'M NOT GOING TO PUT UP WITH THIS A DAY LONGER.

317
00:18:09,192 --> 00:18:10,912
| WARNED MARILLA NOT TO LET IT HAPPEN AGAIN.

318
00:18:11,194 --> 00:18:12,821
WELL, IT HAS.

319
00:18:13,196 --> 00:18:14,823
PATIENCE HAS CEASED TO BE A VIRTUE.

320
00:18:15,198 --> 00:18:16,825
|WANT THIS RUMPUS STOPPED RIGHT NOW.

321
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:19,828
IF YOU COULD JUST CALM DOWN AND TELL ME WHAT THE TROUBLE IS.

322
00:18:20,203 --> 00:18:21,830
HAH! CALM DOWN.

323
00:18:22,205 --> 00:18:24,833
FIRST IT WAS OUR POTATOES. THEN MY JUNE LILIES,

324
00:18:25,208 --> 00:18:27,836
WHICH THOMAS PLANTED ON OUR 25th WEDDING ANNIVERSARY.

325
00:18:28,211 --> 00:18:30,839
NOW THIS DARN JERSEY COW HAS DEVOURED ALMOST

326
00:18:31,214 --> 00:18:32,414
ALL MY PRIZE-WINNING CABBAGES.

327
00:18:33,050 --> 00:18:34,193
AND IF TILLIE BOULTER WALKS AWAY WITH

328
00:18:34,217 --> 00:18:36,057
THE RED RIBBON AT THE CHARLOTTETOWN EXHIBITION,

329
00:18:36,470 --> 00:18:39,848
YOU CAN LET MARILLA KNOW | AM HOLDING HER FINANCIALLY RESPONSIBLE.

330
00:18:40,223 --> 00:18:42,851
'M SORRY, MRS. LYNDE, BECAUSE DOLLY IS MY COW, NOT MARILLA"S.

331
00:18:43,226 --> 00:18:45,812
MATTHEW BOUGHT HER FOR ME TWO YEARS AGO AS A CALF FROM MR. BELL.

332
00:18:46,104 --> 00:18:49,316
SORRY! WELL, SORRY IS NOT GOING TO HELP THE HAVOC

333
00:18:49,650 --> 00:18:51,650
THIS ANIMAL HAS MADE TRAMPLING THROUGH MY CABBAGES.

334
00:18:51,693 --> 00:18:52,670
AND IF YOU THINK...

335
00:18:52,694 --> 00:18:53,671
| AM SORRY.

336
00:18:53,695 --> 00:18:55,495
BUT THE FENCE THAT SEPARATES YOUR POTATO FIELD

337
00:18:55,697 --> 00:18:57,366
FROM OUR PASTURE IS AN EYESORE.

338
00:18:57,699 --> 00:18:58,676
AND IF YOU KEPT IT INBETTER REPAIR,

339
00:18:58,700 --> 00:18:59,900
DOLLY WOULDN'T HAVE BROKEN IN.

340
00:19:00,202 --> 00:19:02,537
A JAIL FENCE WOULDN'T KEEP THAT DEVIL OUT.

341
00:19:03,246 --> 00:19:06,458
AND WHAT'S MORE, MY THOMAS HAS BEEN FAR TOO ILL THE PAST SIX MONTHS

342
00:19:06,792 --> 00:19:07,792
TO REPAIR ANY FENCES.

343
00:19:08,043 --> 00:19:11,463
AND | KNOW ONE THING, YOU RED-HEADED SNIPPET,

344
00:19:11,797 --> 00:19:14,466
YOU'D BE BETTER EMPLOYED FIXING THAT FENCE YOURSELF

345
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:15,880
RATHER THAN MOONING AROUND,

346
00:19:15,926 --> 00:19:18,553
WASTING YOUR TIME WRITING FOR SOME RUBBISHY MAGAZINE.

347
00:19:18,929 --> 00:19:20,529
| WOULD RATHER SPEND MY TIME PROFITABLY,

348
00:19:20,806 --> 00:19:22,474
THAN SQUANDER IT IN IDLE GOSSIP

349
00:19:22,808 --> 00:19:24,208
MEDDLING IN OTHER PEOPLE'S AFFAIRS.

350
00:19:24,351 --> 00:19:25,477
OH!

351
00:19:25,811 --> 00:19:27,571
| WON'T CHERISH ANY HARD FEELINGS AGAINST YOU

352
00:19:27,813 --> 00:19:29,481
BECAUSE OF YOUR NARROW-MINDED OPINIONS.

353
00:19:29,815 --> 00:19:31,483
NOTHANK GOODNESS | HAVE AN IMAGINATION

354
00:19:31,817 --> 00:19:32,835
WHICH ALLOWS ME TO UNDERSTAND

355
00:19:32,859 --> 00:19:35,487
HOW IT MUST BE TO FIND A COW AMONGST PRIZE-WINNING CABBAGES.

356
00:19:35,821 --> 00:19:38,490
DOLLY SHALL NEVER BREAK INTO YOUR FIELD AGAIN.

357
00:19:38,824 --> 00:19:40,492
| GIVE YOU MY WORD OF HONOUR

358
00:19:40,826 --> 00:19:42,744
ON THAT POINT. WELL!

359
00:19:43,286 --> 00:19:44,371
YOU JUST MAKE SURE

360
00:19:44,746 --> 00:19:45,746
THAT SHE DOESN'T.

361
00:19:45,831 --> 00:19:46,998
[ Bawling of cow |.

362
00:19:52,170 --> 00:19:54,715
WHOA. WHOA, WHOA.

363
00:19:55,173 --> 00:19:58,969
WELL, MARILLA, | HOPE THAT CANAL HORSE DESTROYS YOUR TOMATO PATCH NEXT.

364
00:19:59,302 --> 00:20:01,062
AND DON'T EXPECT ANY SYMPATHY FROM YOUR GIRL.

365
00:20:01,304 --> 00:20:04,099
"VE ALWAYS WARNED YOU SHE HAD A TEMPER TO MATCH HER HAIR."

366
00:20:06,268 --> 00:20:07,978
[Thinking ] OH, GOOD LORD.

367
00:20:08,311 --> 00:20:09,311
[ Clicking of tongue |]

368
00:20:12,190 --> 00:20:13,292
SHE CAN'T POSSIBLY GET OUT NOW

369
00:20:13,316 --> 00:20:14,985
UNLESS SHE TEARS THE FENCE DOWN.

370
00:20:15,318 --> 00:20:17,821
| NEVER REALIZED MRS. LYNDE WAS SUCH A CRANK.

371
00:20:18,196 --> 00:20:20,276
THERE'S CERTAINLY NOTHING OF A KINDRED SPIRIT IN HER.

372
00:20:20,323 --> 00:20:28,323
(music)

373
00:20:30,333 --> 00:20:32,294
YOU SET YOUR HEART TOO MUCH ON FRIVOLOUS THINGS,

374
00:20:32,836 --> 00:20:35,005
AND THEN CRASH DOWN INTO DESPAIR

375
00:20:35,338 --> 00:20:37,007
WHEN YOU DON'T GET THEM. |KNOW.

376
00:20:37,340 --> 00:20:41,011
| CAN'T HELP FLYING UP ON THE WINGS OF ANTICIPATION.

377
00:20:41,344 --> 00:20:43,180
IT'S AS GLORIOUS AS SOARING THROUGH A SUNSET.

378
00:20:43,472 --> 00:20:46,016
ALMOST PAYS FOR THE THUD.

379
00:20:46,349 --> 00:20:47,326
WELL, MAYBE IT DOES,

380
00:20:47,350 --> 00:20:50,020
BUT I'D RATHER WALK CALMLY ALONG,

381
00:20:50,353 --> 00:20:54,024
AND DO WITHOUT BOTH FLYING AND THUD.

382
00:20:54,357 --> 00:20:57,235
[ Ringing of cow bells |.

383
00:20:57,736 --> 00:21:00,030
Anne: MARTIN'S FORGOTTEN THE COWS ON ORCHARD SLOPE.

384
00:21:01,948 --> 00:21:03,116
| WAS AS POLITE AS | COULD BE

385
00:21:03,450 --> 00:21:05,118
UNDER THE CIRCUM-STANCES, MARILLA.

386
00:21:05,452 --> 00:21:06,452
AND | APOLOGIZED,

387
00:21:06,578 --> 00:21:09,247
DESPITE HER STINGING PERSONAL REMARKS.

388
00:21:09,581 --> 00:21:13,126
RACHEL SPECIALIZES IN GETTING UNDER PEOPLE'S SKIN, | KNOW,

389
00:21:13,460 --> 00:21:15,180
BUT YOU OUGHT TO HAVE BIT YOUR TONGUE, ANNE,

390
00:21:15,462 --> 00:21:18,131
SEEING AS WE WERE IN THE WRONG.

391
00:21:18,465 --> 00:21:21,134
NO, |OQUGHT TO HAVE SOLD DOLLY TO GILBERT'S FATHER A MONTH AGO

392
00:21:21,468 --> 00:21:23,136
WHEN HE WANTED TO BUY HER.

393
00:21:23,470 --> 00:21:25,448
| THOUGHT IT WAS JUST AS WELL TO WAIT TILL THE AUCTION,

394
00:21:25,472 --> 00:21:27,140
AND LET ALL THE STOCK GO TOGETHER.

395
00:21:27,474 --> 00:21:30,268
MARTIN, THERE ARE TWO MORE COWS.

396
00:21:32,187 --> 00:21:34,022
RACHEL WILL GET OVER THIS.

397
00:21:34,314 --> 00:21:37,984
HER NERVES HAVE BEEN RAW LATELY, AND DESERVEDLY SO.

398
00:21:38,318 --> 00:21:41,988
THOMAS IS PRETTY BAD, AND DR. SPENCER SAYS

399
00:21:42,322 --> 00:21:44,115
THAT HE WON'T BE WITH US FOR VE LONG.

400
00:21:47,994 --> 00:21:49,913
| HOPE SHE DOESN'T HAVE TO SELL HER FARM.

401
00:21:50,247 --> 00:21:51,456
ITDBEA TERRIBLE LOSS.

402
00:21:51,832 --> 00:21:53,500
AND | KNOW HOW WE FELT WHEN MATTHEW DIED.

403
00:21:53,834 --> 00:21:57,045
ANNE, I'VE WANTED TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT SOMETHING FOR A WHILE.

404
00:21:57,337 --> 00:22:00,590
|IKNOW YOU'VE BEEN CONTENT ENOUGH HERE,

405
00:22:00,924 --> 00:22:03,552
BUT | NEVER FEEL AT EASE,

406
00:22:03,927 --> 00:22:07,764
THINKING ABOUT HOW YOU HAVE GIVEN UP SO MUCH OF YOUR OWN OPPORTUNITY.

407
00:22:08,265 --> 00:22:12,602
MARILLA, | COULDN'T LEAVE YOU ALONE HERE.

408
00:22:12,936 --> 00:22:15,056
BESIDES, I'M... 'D PROBABLY MAKE A MUCH BETTER TEACHER

409
00:22:15,313 --> 00:22:18,608
THAN A WRITER ANY DAY. ANNE...

410
00:22:18,942 --> 00:22:20,569
YOU HAVE BEEN MY COMFORT AND MY JOY

411
00:22:20,944 --> 00:22:22,487
SINCE MATTHEW PASSED AWAY.

412
00:22:24,155 --> 00:22:25,574
BUT | PROMISED MYSELF

413
00:22:25,949 --> 00:22:28,493
WHEN YOU GAVE UP THE AVERY SCHOLARSHIP TO STAY HOME,

414
00:22:28,827 --> 00:22:30,579
'D MAKE IT UP TO YOU ONE DAY.

415
00:22:30,954 --> 00:22:33,331
"VE NEVER BEEN SORRY I'VE STAYED FOR A MOMENT."

416
00:22:38,461 --> 00:22:42,007
MR. BARRY HAS REALLY TAKEN OVER THE FARM ALMOST COMPLETELY AND...

417
00:22:42,465 --> 00:22:43,693
MY EYESIGHT IS SOQ MUCH BETTER NOW,

418
00:22:43,717 --> 00:22:46,136
| CAN MANAGE WITH MARTIN.

419
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:49,222
PERHAPS ONE OF THE PICARD GIRLS OVER IN RUSTICO

420
00:22:49,514 --> 00:22:51,683
COULD... BOARD WITH ME FOR A WHILE,

421
00:22:52,434 --> 00:22:56,354
SO YOU COULD DUST OFF SOME OF YOUR AMBITIONS IF YOU LIKE.

422
00:22:56,646 --> 00:22:58,189
WHAT DO YOU THINK ABOUT THAT?

423
00:22:58,481 --> 00:22:59,481
OH, MARILLA!

424
00:22:59,524 --> 00:23:02,319
| FEEL AS THOUGH SOMEONE'S HANDED ME THE MOON,

425
00:23:02,611 --> 00:23:04,331
AND | DON'T EXACTLY KNOW WHAT TO DO WITH IT.

426
00:23:05,947 --> 00:23:08,325
MATTHEW AND | SPENT 40 YEARS LOOKING AFTER PAPA.

427
00:23:08,617 --> 00:23:11,328
PERHAPS | NEVER MENTIONED IT BEFORE, BUT...

428
00:23:11,620 --> 00:23:13,330
| CAN'T HELP BUT CONFESS,

429
00:23:13,622 --> 00:23:16,249
IT WAS WITH A REGRETFUL HEART AT TIMES.

430
00:23:17,792 --> 00:23:21,338
YOU HAD A LITTLE BIT OF ROMANCE IN YOUR OWN LIFE, MARILLA.

431
00:23:21,630 --> 00:23:23,470
YOU WOULDN'T THINK IT TO LOOK AT ME, WOULD YOU?

432
00:23:23,632 --> 00:23:27,344
BUT YOU CAN NEVER TELL ABOUT PEOPLE BY THEIR OUTSIDES.

433
00:23:27,636 --> 00:23:32,349
DO YOU SUPPOSE THAT MR. BLYTHE REMEMBERS THAT HE WAS YOUR BEAU?

434
00:23:32,641 --> 00:23:34,351
STUFF AND NONSENSE. [ Giggling ]

435
00:23:34,643 --> 00:23:37,354
NO, NO. THAT'S ENOUGH NOW.

436
00:23:37,646 --> 00:23:38,646
NO MORE FOOLISHNESS.

437
00:23:39,314 --> 00:23:42,359
OH, IT SEEMS SO FUNNY AND HORRIBLE

438
00:23:42,651 --> 00:23:45,362
TO THINK OF DIANA MARRYING FRED, DOESN'T IT?

439
00:23:45,654 --> 00:23:47,364
WHAT IS SO HORRIBLE ABOUT IT?

440
00:23:47,656 --> 00:23:50,367
WELL, HE CERTAINLY ISN'T THE WILD, DASHING YOUNG MAN

441
00:23:50,659 --> 00:23:52,452
DIANA USED TO WANT TO MARRY.

442
00:23:53,703 --> 00:23:54,703
FRED IS...

443
00:23:55,372 --> 00:23:56,915
EXTREMELY GOOD.

444
00:23:57,374 --> 00:23:59,918
THAT IS EXACTLY WHAT HE SHOULD BE.

445
00:24:01,211 --> 00:24:03,964
WOULD YOU WANT TO MARRY A WICKED MAN?

446
00:24:04,297 --> 00:24:08,093
WELL, |WOULDN'T MARRY ANYONE WHO WAS REALLY WICKED.

447
00:24:08,426 --> 00:24:10,971
BUT | THINK I'D LIKE IT IF HE COULD BE WICKED...

448
00:24:11,304 --> 00:24:12,281
AND WOULDN'T.

449
00:24:12,305 --> 00:24:17,978
(music)

450
00:24:18,311 --> 00:24:20,105
YOU'LL HAVE MORE SENSE SOMEDAY, | HOPE.

451
00:24:21,648 --> 00:24:23,942
| BELIEVE ANNE SHIRLEY JUST COPIED THAT STORY.

452
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:27,487
| AM SURE | REMEMBER READING IT IN A NEWSPAPER YEARS AGO.

453
00:24:27,821 --> 00:24:30,740
WELL, I'M SORRY TO HEAR SHE'S TAKEN TO WRITING NOVELS AT ALL.

454
00:24:31,491 --> 00:24:33,576
NOBODY BORN AND BRED IN AVONLEA WOULD DOIT.

455
00:24:35,662 --> 00:24:38,415
BEEN WRITING ANY MORE STORIES LATELY, MISS SHIRLEY?

456
00:24:38,707 --> 00:24:40,500
NO, MRS. HARRISON.

457
00:24:40,834 --> 00:24:42,502
WELL, NO OFFENSE MEANT.

458
00:24:42,836 --> 00:24:45,716
MABEL SLOANE HERE SAYS SHE FOUND ANOTHER ONE OF THEM BIG MANILA ENVELOPES

459
00:24:45,839 --> 00:24:47,775
COME THROUGH HERE A COUPLE OF WEEKS AGO, THAT'S ALL.

460
00:24:47,799 --> 00:24:48,818
HMM, IT WAS ADDRESSED TO THE

461
00:24:48,842 --> 00:24:51,511
ROLLING RELIABLE BAKING POWDER COMPANY IN MONTREAL.

462
00:24:51,845 --> 00:24:54,556
| SUSPICIONED THAT SOMEBODY WAS TRYING FOR THAT PRIZE

463
00:24:54,889 --> 00:24:57,517
THAT THEY'RE OFFERING FOR THE BEST STORY

464
00:24:57,851 --> 00:24:59,602
INTRODUCING THEIR NEW BAKING POWDER.

465
00:24:59,936 --> 00:25:02,522
THE ADDRESS WASN'T IN YOUR HANDWRITING THOUGH.

466
00:25:02,897 --> 00:25:04,607
| SHOULD HOPE NOT.

467
00:25:04,941 --> 00:25:08,153
I'D NEVER DREAM OF COMPETING FOR ANYTHING SO DISGRACEFUL.

468
00:25:08,528 --> 00:25:12,615
IT WOULD ALMOST BE AS BAD AS JAKE GRIFFITH'S CHATAGHUA SHOW.

469
00:25:12,949 --> 00:25:15,618
BUT THEN THAT'S WHAT COMES OF MARILLA CUTHBERT ADOPTING AN ORPHAN

470
00:25:15,952 --> 00:25:18,621
FROM GOODNESS KNOWS WHERE, OR WHAT KIND OF PARENTS.

471
00:25:18,955 --> 00:25:19,955
OH!

472
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:23,710
WHY, ANNE, CONGRATULATIONS.

473
00:25:25,253 --> 00:25:27,714
YOU HAVE SUCH A WAY OF PUTTING AVONLEA ON THE MAP.

474
00:25:28,048 --> 00:25:29,632
WELL... THANK YOU.

475
00:25:29,966 --> 00:25:30,966
BUT WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

476
00:25:32,594 --> 00:25:34,596
CONGRATULATIONS FOR WHAT?

477
00:25:34,929 --> 00:25:38,266
[ Sarcastic laugh | YOU WERE ALWAYS SUCH A TERRIBLE FAKE AT MODESTY, ANNE,

478
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:39,642
EVEN DURING PUBLIC SCHOOL.

479
00:25:39,976 --> 00:25:41,736
WELL, THERE'S NOTHING FAKE ABOUT THE BUSINESS

480
00:25:42,145 --> 00:25:44,647
LAWSON'S GENERAL STORE INTENDS TO DO FROM ALLTHIS.

481
00:25:45,356 --> 00:25:47,108
AND | THINK THAT BLUE YOU'RE WEARING

482
00:25:47,442 --> 00:25:49,652
IS SO DRAMATIC FOR A YOUNG AUTHORESS.

483
00:25:49,986 --> 00:25:52,113
YOU ALMOST LOOK PRETTY INIT.

484
00:25:52,655 --> 00:25:53,656
[ Sarcastic chuckle |.

485
00:25:53,990 --> 00:25:55,742
DON'T SAY THINGS YOU DON'T MEAN, JOSIE.

486
00:25:56,868 --> 00:25:59,204
THAT ANNE SHIRLEY IS SO SMUG.

487
00:26:00,497 --> 00:26:02,540
THAT GIRL ALWAYS DID GIVE HERSELF AIRS.

488
00:26:05,335 --> 00:26:06,586
Boys: CONGRATULATIONS.

489
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:07,920
CONGRATULATIONS, ANNE.

490
00:26:08,254 --> 00:26:09,464
IT'S AWONDERFUL STORY, ANNE.

491
00:26:09,964 --> 00:26:11,257
CONGRATULATIONS.

492
00:26:12,634 --> 00:26:14,177
WONDERFUL STORY, ANNE.

493
00:26:14,511 --> 00:26:15,511
YOU DESERVE THE BEST.

494
00:26:18,348 --> 00:26:20,468
Women: CONGRATULATIONS. CONGRATULATIONS, MISS SHIRLEY.

495
00:26:20,517 --> 00:26:23,186
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR STORY, MISS SHIRLEY.

496
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:25,271
| REALLY LIKE THE BIT ABOUT THE CAKE.

497
00:26:27,357 --> 00:26:32,195
(music)

498
00:26:32,529 --> 00:26:34,280
GREAT JEHOSOPHAT!

499
00:26:36,366 --> 00:26:38,284
[ Excited murmurs |.

500
00:26:45,792 --> 00:26:49,212
ANNE SHIRLEY, WE'VE BEEN TRYING TO TRACK YOU DOWN EVERYWHERE.

501
00:26:49,546 --> 00:26:51,714
OH, LADIES AND GENTLEMEN, MAY | PRESENT TO YOU

502
00:26:52,132 --> 00:26:54,300
AVONLEA'S FAMOUS AUTHORESS.

503
00:27:00,807 --> 00:27:02,392
FATHER, COME OUT HERE.

504
00:27:08,481 --> 00:27:10,400
OH, MY GOODNESS, MISS SHIRLEY.

505
00:27:11,860 --> 00:27:13,319
| DON'T UNDERSTAND.

506
00:27:13,653 --> 00:27:15,321
YOU WON THE CONTEST, YOU GOOSE.

507
00:27:15,655 --> 00:27:17,615
AND | KNEW YOU'D GO AND DOIT ALL BEHIND OUR BACKS.

508
00:27:17,907 --> 00:27:19,627
Mr. Lawson: QUIET, EVERYBODY, QUIET PLEASE.

509
00:27:19,659 --> 00:27:21,637
[ Clearing of throat ] [ Ringing of cash register bell ]

510
00:27:21,661 --> 00:27:23,329
IT IS MY GREAT PLEASURE

511
00:27:23,663 --> 00:27:26,332
AS OFFICIAL PURVEYOR TO AVONLEA

512
00:27:26,666 --> 00:27:29,335
OF THE ROLLINGS RELIABLE BAKING POWDER COMPANY

513
00:27:29,669 --> 00:27:33,339
TO READ THIS, THE FOLLOWING TRIBUTE.

514
00:27:33,673 --> 00:27:34,674
UH, MISS ANNE SHIRLEY,

515
00:27:35,216 --> 00:27:37,343
GREEN GABLES, PEI.

516
00:27:37,677 --> 00:27:38,654
DEAR MADAM,

517
00:27:38,678 --> 00:27:41,347
WE HAVE MUCH PLEASURE IN INFORMING YOU

518
00:27:41,681 --> 00:27:45,268
THAT YOUR CHARMING STORY, "AVERILS ATONEMENT,"

519
00:27:45,643 --> 00:27:48,354
[ Applause ] HAS WON THE $100 GRAND PRIZE.

520
00:27:48,688 --> 00:27:51,274
INOQUR RECENT COMPETI-TION FOR THE BEST STORY

521
00:27:51,649 --> 00:27:54,360
INTRODUCING THE NAME OF OUR REVERED PRODUCT.

522
00:27:54,694 --> 00:27:55,945
[ Applause ] [ Chuckling ]

523
00:27:57,530 --> 00:28:00,450
UH, THE PRIZE WILL BE PRESENTED BY MR. CHARLES LAWSON

524
00:28:00,783 --> 00:28:01,943
OF LAWSON'S GENERAL, AVONLEA.

525
00:28:03,953 --> 00:28:06,456
WE HAVE ARRANGED PUBLICATION OF THE STORY

526
00:28:06,789 --> 00:28:09,959
IN SEVERAL PROMINENT NEWSPAPERS ACROSS THE COUNTRY,

527
00:28:10,460 --> 00:28:12,545
AND WILL SUPPLY IT INPAMPHLET FORM

528
00:28:12,879 --> 00:28:15,465
FOR DISTRIBUTION AMONG OUR PATRONS.

529
00:28:15,798 --> 00:28:17,759
THANKING YOU FOR THE INTEREST YOU HAVE SHOWN

530
00:28:18,134 --> 00:28:19,469
IN SUPPORTING OUR ENTERPRISES,

531
00:28:19,802 --> 00:28:22,472
WE REMAIN YOURS VERY TRULY

532
00:28:22,805 --> 00:28:25,475
THE ROLLINGS RELIABLE...

533
00:28:25,808 --> 00:28:27,518
BAKING POWDER COMPANY.

534
00:28:30,146 --> 00:28:32,565
YOU'LL SIGN MINE, WON'T YOU? HERE

535
00:28:33,024 --> 00:28:35,485
OH, AND I'M SURE MISS SHIRLEY WILL BE HAPPY

536
00:28:35,818 --> 00:28:36,795
TO SIGN EVERYBODY'S BROCHURES.

537
00:28:36,819 --> 00:28:40,281
AND DON'T FORGET YOUR PURCHASE OF THIS REMARKABLE PRODUCT.

538
00:28:40,615 --> 00:28:41,615
NEXT. ANNE!

539
00:28:43,660 --> 00:28:46,496
OH, /M WILD WITH DELIGHT. AH!

540
00:28:46,829 --> 00:28:49,582
| WAS SURE IT WOULD WIN WHEN | SENT IT INTO THE COMPETITION.

541
00:28:50,667 --> 00:28:52,502
DIANA BARRY! YES | DID.

542
00:28:52,835 --> 00:28:54,504
| THOUGHT OF YOUR STORY IN A MINUTE

543
00:28:54,837 --> 00:28:56,506
WHEN | SAW THE AD IN THE PAPER.

544
00:28:56,839 --> 00:28:58,901
Man: MISS SHIRLEY, WILL YOU SIGN THIS FOR MY DAUGHTER?

545
00:28:58,925 --> 00:29:00,677
[ Mixed hubbub |.

546
00:29:00,969 --> 00:29:01,969
THANK YOU.

547
00:29:02,011 --> 00:29:03,989
WELL | WAS GOING TO TELL YOU TO SEND IT IN YOURSELF,

548
00:29:04,013 --> 00:29:06,493
BUT | FIGURED YOU HAD SO LITTLE FAITH LEFT IN IT, YOU WOULDN'T.

549
00:29:06,599 --> 00:29:07,684
SO | SENT MY COPY.

550
00:29:08,017 --> 00:29:09,817
THEN IF IT HADN'T WON, YOU'D NEVER HAVE KNOWN,

551
00:29:10,019 --> 00:29:12,219
BECAUSE THE STORIES THAT FAILED WEREN'T BEING SENT BACK.

552
00:29:16,776 --> 00:29:19,612
WHY, ANNE, YOU DON'T SEEM A BIT PLEASED.

553
00:29:19,946 --> 00:29:22,490
OF COURSE | COULDN'T BE ANYTHING BUT PLEASED.

554
00:29:22,824 --> 00:29:24,134
IT WAS THE GESTUREOF A TRUE FRIEND

555
00:29:24,158 --> 00:29:25,702
TO TRY TO BOOST MY SPIRITS.

556
00:29:26,327 --> 00:29:28,246
BUT THERE ISN'T A WORD ABOUT...

557
00:29:29,205 --> 00:29:30,873
BAKING POWDER.

558
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:32,875
OH, | PUT THAT IN. IT WAS EASY AS A WINK.

559
00:29:33,167 --> 00:29:35,007
YOU KNOW THE SCENE WHERE AVERIL MAKES THE CAKE?

560
00:29:35,169 --> 00:29:37,147
WELL, | JUST STATED THAT SHE USED ROLLINGS RELIABLE,

561
00:29:37,171 --> 00:29:38,881
AND THAT'S WHY IT TURNED OUT SO WELL.

562
00:29:39,173 --> 00:29:40,883
SEE? AND THE HERE, IN THE LAST PARAGRAPH

563
00:29:41,384 --> 00:29:44,721
WHERE PERCIVAL CLASPS AVERIL IN HIS ARMS AND SAYS.

564
00:29:45,054 --> 00:29:46,723
"SWEETHEART, THE BEAUTIFUL COMING YEARS"

565
00:29:47,056 --> 00:29:49,726
"WILL BRING US THE FULFILMENT OF OUR HOUSE OF DREAMS."

566
00:29:50,310 --> 00:29:53,104
| ADDED, "IN WHICH WE WILL NEVER USE ANY BAKING POWDER"

567
00:29:53,438 --> 00:29:55,148
"EXCEPT ROLLINGS RELIABLE."

568
00:29:56,607 --> 00:29:57,775
OH-H!

569
00:29:58,943 --> 00:30:00,743
COME ON. | HAVE THE BUGGY. I'LL TAKE YOU HOME.

570
00:30:01,070 --> 00:30:03,740
(music)

571
00:30:04,073 --> 00:30:05,742
YOU'VE WON $100.

572
00:30:06,075 --> 00:30:07,875
AND PRISSY GRANT TOLD ME THAT "CANADIAN WOMEN"

573
00:30:08,077 --> 00:30:10,038
ONLY PAID $5 A STORY.

574
00:30:13,541 --> 00:30:16,919
| CAN'T TAKE IT. IT'S RIGHTFULLY YOURS, DIANA.

575
00:30:17,211 --> 00:30:19,339
YOU SENT THE STORY IN AND MADE THE ALTERATIONS.

576
00:30:19,922 --> 00:30:22,592
| CERTAINLY WOULDN'T HAVE SENT IT.

577
00:30:22,967 --> 00:30:23,967
SO YOU HAVE TO TAKE IT.

578
00:30:24,177 --> 00:30:25,678
I'D LIKE TO SEE MYSELF!

579
00:30:25,970 --> 00:30:27,847
IT WASN'T ANY TROUBLE, ANNE.

580
00:30:28,139 --> 00:30:30,117
THE HONOUR OF BEING THE BEST FRIEND OF THE PRIZE WINNER

581
00:30:30,141 --> 00:30:31,851
IS ENOUGH FOR ME

582
00:30:32,143 --> 00:30:33,770
I'M SO GLAD FOR YOUR SAKE.

583
00:30:37,565 --> 00:30:39,484
| THINK YOU'RE THE SWEETEST AND TRUEST FRIEND

584
00:30:39,901 --> 00:30:41,486
IN THE WORLD, DIANA.

585
00:30:41,903 --> 00:30:43,463
| WILL BUY YOUR WEDDING GIFT WITH THIS.

586
00:30:43,780 --> 00:30:45,865
DON'T YOU DARE SPEND IT ALL ON ME.

587
00:30:46,366 --> 00:30:49,911
| GOT A LETTER TODAY FROM OUR DEAR OLD TEACHER, MISS STACEY.

588
00:30:50,370 --> 00:30:53,373
SHE IS HEAD OF THE KING'S COUNTY BOARD OF EDUCATION IN NEW BRUNSWICK.

589
00:30:53,706 --> 00:30:56,376
WHAT A PROMOTION. WELL, APPARENTLY,

590
00:30:56,709 --> 00:30:59,379
THERE'S A POSITION SHE'S RECOMMENDED ME FOR

591
00:30:59,712 --> 00:31:01,464
AT ALADIES' COLLEGE IN KINGSPORT.

592
00:31:01,798 --> 00:31:03,466
HOW FLATTERING!

593
00:31:03,800 --> 00:31:05,468
YOU WOULDN'T ACTUALLY LEAVE, WOULD YOU?

594
00:31:05,802 --> 00:31:08,513
NO, BUT | OUGHT TO REPLY ANYWAY.

595
00:31:08,888 --> 00:31:10,473
SHE'S GONE TO ALL THIS TROUBLE,

596
00:31:10,807 --> 00:31:12,167
AND | WOULD... [ Bawling of cow |]

597
00:31:13,684 --> 00:31:15,478
STOP, DIANA!

598
00:31:15,812 --> 00:31:17,105
ANNE!

599
00:31:17,605 --> 00:31:18,605
YOU'LL RUIN YOUR DRESS

600
00:31:18,815 --> 00:31:19,975
IN THAT MUDDY FIELD. RUIN IT!

601
00:31:21,275 --> 00:31:23,903
OH, SHE'LL NEVER GET THAT COW OUT BY HERSELF.

602
00:31:24,695 --> 00:31:30,493
(music)

603
00:31:30,827 --> 00:31:31,827
COME BACK!

604
00:31:34,205 --> 00:31:35,205
STOP!

605
00:31:38,126 --> 00:31:40,503
ANNE SHIRLEY, YOU'RE BEING RIDICULOUS.

606
00:31:40,837 --> 00:31:43,506
GET OUT OF THIS FIELD THIS MINUTE.

607
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:45,633
| DON'T CARE ABOUT MY DRESS.

608
00:31:49,178 --> 00:31:52,640
| MUST GET THE COW OUT BEFORE RACHEL LYNDE SEES HER.

609
00:31:57,019 --> 00:31:59,355
GO ON, DIANA, RUN.

610
00:31:59,730 --> 00:32:00,731
CORNER HER.

611
00:32:02,817 --> 00:32:04,610
THAT'S IT, DIANA.

612
00:32:04,944 --> 00:32:06,028
NOW DON'T FRIGHTEN HER.

613
00:32:11,033 --> 00:32:13,202
THIS IS WHAT WE'VE GOT TO DO.

614
00:32:13,536 --> 00:32:14,662
[ Bawling of cow |.

615
00:32:15,037 --> 00:32:16,397
MAYBE IF WE CAN GET A HOLD OF HER,

616
00:32:16,456 --> 00:32:19,167
WE CAN FORCE HER OVER THE FENCE INTO OUR FIELD.

617
00:32:19,667 --> 00:32:21,461
OKAY, YOU FILL THE GAP,

618
00:32:21,836 --> 00:32:23,147
AND I'M GOING TO MAKE A RUN FORIT,

619
00:32:23,171 --> 00:32:24,148
STRAIGHT TOWARDS HER.

620
00:32:24,172 --> 00:32:25,840
WITH ANY LUCK, SHE'LL JUMP THE FENCE.

621
00:32:26,174 --> 00:32:27,151
YOU DON'T MEAN YOU'RE GOING TO ACTUALLY

622
00:32:27,175 --> 00:32:28,843
WALK THROUGH THAT MULCH, DO YOU?

623
00:32:29,635 --> 00:32:31,846
IT'S THE LESSER OF THE TWO EVILS, DIANA.

624
00:32:32,180 --> 00:32:34,932
WHAT IF SHE WAS GOING TO GET INTO RACHELS CABBAGE PATCH AGAIN?

625
00:32:35,892 --> 00:32:40,688
(music)

626
00:32:48,070 --> 00:32:50,865
ALL RIGHT, | HAVE THE GAP BLOCKED.

627
00:32:51,199 --> 00:32:52,867
COME HERE, DOLLY.

628
00:32:53,201 --> 00:32:54,869
GOOD GIRL.

629
00:32:55,203 --> 00:32:56,996
SHOO. COME ON.

630
00:32:57,663 --> 00:32:59,040
WRETCHED COW.

631
00:33:02,168 --> 00:33:04,879
OH, DON'T EVEN THINK ABOUT RACHELS CABBAGES.

632
00:33:05,171 --> 00:33:06,148
[ Gasp |

633
00:33:06,172 --> 00:33:07,172
[ Shriek ]

634
00:33:13,179 --> 00:33:14,889
COME HERE, YOU STUPID...

635
00:33:15,181 --> 00:33:16,891
Both: [ Yelping ]

636
00:33:17,183 --> 00:33:18,160
[ Whimpering ]

637
00:33:18,184 --> 00:33:20,978
[ Sigh ] SORRY.

638
00:33:21,562 --> 00:33:22,562
Gil: WELL,

639
00:33:22,897 --> 00:33:24,899
THE ELEGANT AND ILLUSTRIOUS MISS SHIRLEY.

640
00:33:25,191 --> 00:33:26,901
UH, RELAXED WHILE SEEKING OUT IDEAS

641
00:33:27,193 --> 00:33:28,903
FOR HER NEXT ROLLING RELIABLE'S...

642
00:33:29,195 --> 00:33:30,905
WRITING ASSIGNMENT, | PRESUME.

643
00:33:31,197 --> 00:33:33,908
WELL, DO YOU SUPPOSE I'M HERE TO CHAT WITH THE BULLFROGS?

644
00:33:34,242 --> 00:33:35,242
BE A GENTLEMAN.

645
00:33:39,205 --> 00:33:40,891
YOU'D HAVE BEEN BETTER OFF SELLING HER LAST MONTH

646
00:33:40,915 --> 00:33:42,035
WHEN DAD OFFERED TO BUY HER.

647
00:33:42,208 --> 00:33:45,002
WELL, I'LL SELL DOLLY TO HIM RIGHT NOW IF HE WANTS HER.

648
00:33:46,128 --> 00:33:47,128
Man: [ Laughing ]

649
00:33:49,799 --> 00:33:51,384
YOU MAY HAVE OUR DARN JERSEY

650
00:33:51,884 --> 00:33:53,244
ANY TIME YOU WANT HER, MR. BLYTHE.

651
00:33:53,344 --> 00:33:55,054
THIS VERY MINUTE FOR THAT MATTER.

652
00:33:55,346 --> 00:33:57,932
[ Laughing heartily | DONE!

653
00:33:58,224 --> 00:34:02,019
LL GIVE YOU THE $20 | OFFERED BEFORE.

654
00:34:02,311 --> 00:34:04,031
GIL CAN DRIVE HER OVER TO CARMODY RIGHT NOW.

655
00:34:04,272 --> 00:34:06,291
SHE'LL GO TO TOWN WITH THE REST OF THE SHIPMENT THIS EVENING.

656
00:34:06,315 --> 00:34:09,026
| PROMISED MR. REED OF BRIGHTON A JERSEY.

657
00:34:09,318 --> 00:34:11,737
[ Chuckling ]

658
00:34:12,488 --> 00:34:14,031
WHAT WILL MARILLA SAY?

659
00:34:14,323 --> 00:34:15,408
SHE WON'T CARE.

660
00:34:16,117 --> 00:34:18,035
DOLLY WAS MY COW ANYWAY.

661
00:34:18,327 --> 00:34:22,039
IT'S NOT LIKELY SHE'LL BRING MORE THAN $20 AT THE AUCTION.

662
00:34:22,331 --> 00:34:24,041
BUT WHEN RACHEL SEES THIS FIELD,

663
00:34:24,333 --> 00:34:26,043
SHE'LL KNOW DOLLY WAS LOOSE.

664
00:34:26,335 --> 00:34:29,046
ANNE, I'LL BE OVER THIS AFTERNOON WITH YOUR $20.

665
00:34:29,338 --> 00:34:31,048
WELL, IT'S TAUGHT ME A LESSON,

666
00:34:31,340 --> 00:34:34,051
NOT TO STAKE MY WORD OF HONOUR ON COWS.

667
00:34:34,343 --> 00:34:36,012
Mr. Blythe: [ Chuckling ]

668
00:34:36,304 --> 00:34:40,016
(music)

669
00:34:40,308 --> 00:34:41,577
HOW DO YOU THINK A MOTHER WOULD FEEL

670
00:34:41,601 --> 00:34:44,020
IF SHE FOUND HER CHILD TATTOOED ALL OVER

671
00:34:44,312 --> 00:34:47,064
WITH A BAKING POWDER ADVERTISEMENT?

672
00:34:47,356 --> 00:34:49,066
| LOVED MY STORY,

673
00:34:49,358 --> 00:34:51,158
AND | WROTE IT OUT OF THE BEST THAT WAS IN ME.

674
00:34:51,652 --> 00:34:53,279
AH, YOU'RE JUST TIRED.

675
00:34:55,740 --> 00:34:58,075
BESIDES, WHY SHOULD YOU CARE?

676
00:34:58,367 --> 00:35:01,162
100 BUCKS IS MORE THAN YOU MAKE IN TWO MONTHS TEACHING ANYWAY.

677
00:35:01,454 --> 00:35:05,166
JOSIE PYE AND TILLIE BOULTER CAN'T WAIT TO POUNCE ON IT.

678
00:35:05,458 --> 00:35:07,168
AH, THEY'RE SPITEFUL OLD CATS.

679
00:35:07,460 --> 00:35:10,171
YOU'RE JUST THE FIRST PERSON IN POKEY OLD AVONLEA

680
00:35:10,463 --> 00:35:11,503
TO TRY ANYTHING LIKE THAT.

681
00:35:16,218 --> 00:35:20,264
ALL PIONEERS ARE CONSIDERED TO BE AFFLICTED WITH MOONSTRUCK MADNESS.

682
00:35:20,848 --> 00:35:22,600
MAD TO THINK | COULD WRITE ANYTHING BETTER

683
00:35:23,017 --> 00:35:24,417
THAN A BAKING POWDER ADVERTISEMENT.

684
00:35:27,229 --> 00:35:31,192
THIS HAS DAMPENED ANY SPARK OF AMBITION.

685
00:35:31,484 --> 00:35:34,111
| SHALL NEVER WRITE ANOTHER STORY AGAIN.

686
00:35:34,403 --> 00:35:36,989
WELL, | WOULDN'T GIVE UP ALTOGETHER.

687
00:35:39,241 --> 00:35:42,203
MAYBE IF YOU JUST LET YOUR CHARACTERS SPEAK EVERYDAY ENGLISH

688
00:35:42,495 --> 00:35:45,206
INSTEAD OF ALL THAT HIGH-FALUTING MUMBO-JUMBO.

689
00:35:45,498 --> 00:35:49,210
YOU THINK MY STORY'S FULL OF FAULTS TOO, DON'T YOU?

690
00:35:49,502 --> 00:35:51,128
"WILT THOU GIVE UP THY GARTER,"

691
00:35:51,420 --> 00:35:53,214
"OH, FAIREST OF THE FAIR?"

692
00:35:53,506 --> 00:35:55,216
ANNE, NOBODY SPEAKS THAT WAY.

693
00:35:55,508 --> 00:35:56,668
AND LOOK AT THAT SAD PERCIVAL

694
00:35:56,759 --> 00:35:58,359
WHO SITS AROUND MOONING THE ENTIRE TIME.

695
00:35:58,511 --> 00:36:00,311
HE NEVER LETS THE GIRL GET A WORD IN EDGEWISE.

696
00:36:01,639 --> 00:36:03,140
IN REAL LIFE, SHE'D HAVE PITCHED HIM.

697
00:36:03,516 --> 00:36:06,060
HIS POETRY WOULD WIN ANY GIRLS HEART.

698
00:36:10,356 --> 00:36:12,149
