| CAN BE CIVIL WITH RACHEL,

1390
01:13:53,784 --> 01:13:55,827
AS LONG AS SHE STAYS OUT OF MY KITCHEN.

1391
01:13:57,496 --> 01:14:01,375
WE'LL BE QUITE CAPABLE OF LOOKING AFTER THE FARM WITH MR. BARRY'S HELP.

1392
01:14:01,792 --> 01:14:02,792
MARILLA...

1393
01:14:04,044 --> 01:14:06,463
DO YOU NEVER WISH YOU'D ADOPTED A BOY

1394
01:14:06,797 --> 01:14:08,465
LIKE YOU INTENDED TO?

1395
01:14:08,799 --> 01:14:10,239
| MEAN, HE COULD HAVE RUN THIS FARM,

1396
01:14:10,634 --> 01:14:12,469
AND SAVED YOU ALL THIS TROUBLE.

1397
01:14:12,803 --> 01:14:17,474
ANNE SHIRLEY, | WOULDN'T TRADE YOU FOR A DOZEN BOYS.

1398
01:14:17,808 --> 01:14:19,559
NOW YOU JUST MIND THAT.

1399
01:14:19,977 --> 01:14:23,313
WAS IT A BOY THAT GOT THE BACHELOR OF ARTS,

1400
01:14:23,647 --> 01:14:26,483
AND WON THE ROLLINGS RELIABLE STORY CONTEST,

1401
01:14:26,817 --> 01:14:27,817
NOW WAS IT?

1402
01:14:28,568 --> 01:14:31,405
LL MISS YOU. "LL MISS MY GIRL."

1403
01:14:32,489 --> 01:14:35,117
PROMISE ME YOU WON'T STAY AWAY FOREVER.

1404
01:14:35,450 --> 01:14:43,450
(music)

1405
01:14:53,218 --> 01:14:55,721
| NEVER THOUGHT OF LIVING AS FAR OFF THE ROAD AS GREEN GABLES,

1406
01:14:56,013 --> 01:14:58,432
BUT I... (D RATHER LIVE AT THE BOTTOM OF A WELL

1407
01:14:58,807 --> 01:14:59,807
THAN LEAVE AVONLEA.

1408
01:14:59,891 --> 01:15:01,977
WELL, | KNOW HOW GRATEFUL ANNE IS TO YOU FOR STAYING.

1409
01:15:02,394 --> 01:15:04,855
WELL, SHE WAS ALWAYS ONE TO LEAP INTO THINGS

1410
01:15:05,188 --> 01:15:06,857
WHEN SHE'D MADE HER MIND UP TOIT.

1411
01:15:07,190 --> 01:15:09,860
IT'S A BLESSING SHE'S OFF TO A LADIES' ACADEMY, THAT'S WHAT.

1412
01:15:10,193 --> 01:15:12,863
| DON'T APPROVE OF THEM CO-EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS,

1413
01:15:13,196 --> 01:15:14,865
AND | NEVER HAVE. ALL THE GIRLS

1414
01:15:15,198 --> 01:15:16,408
FLIRTING WITH ALL THE BOYS.

1415
01:15:17,117 --> 01:15:18,410
THEY DO STUDY A LITTLE, RACHEL.

1416
01:15:18,910 --> 01:15:20,829
HUMPH. PRECIOUS LITTLE.

1417
01:15:21,121 --> 01:15:22,961
HOWEVER HER PUPILS WILL BE WELL ENOUGH BEHAVED,

1418
01:15:23,123 --> 01:15:24,308
IF THIS SCHOOLS AS WELL-TO-DO AS SHE CLAIMS.

1419
01:15:24,332 --> 01:15:26,877
| CAN'T IMAGINE I'VE FORGOTTEN A THING.

1420
01:15:27,252 --> 01:15:28,879
Anne: YOU'VE ALL BEEN SO HELPFUL.

1421
01:15:29,212 --> 01:15:30,372
MIND HOW YOU WERE RAISED NOW,

1422
01:15:30,797 --> 01:15:32,117
AND GO TO CHURCH REGULARLY, ANNE,

1423
01:15:32,215 --> 01:15:33,717
AND BE CAREFUL WHAT FRIENDS YOU MAKE.

1424
01:15:34,009 --> 01:15:36,009
Marilla: BE SURE TO PUT ON YOUR WARM UNDER-CLOTHES.

1425
01:15:36,178 --> 01:15:37,196
WHEN THE WEATHER GETS CHILLY.

1426
01:15:37,220 --> 01:15:39,198
Rachel: YES, AND BE CAREFUL OF YOUR HEALTH WHATEVER YOU DO.

1427
01:15:39,222 --> 01:15:41,558
AND YOU LET US HEAR FROM YOU WHEN YOU'VE SETTLED.

1428
01:15:46,730 --> 01:15:48,523
Rachel: GOODBYE, ANNE. GOODBYE.

1429
01:15:48,857 --> 01:15:49,917
MAKE SURE EVERYTHING'S WELL TAGGED

1430
01:15:49,941 --> 01:15:51,526
WHEN YOU PUT IT ON THE TRAIN.

1431
01:15:51,860 --> 01:15:53,880
DON'T WORRY, WE'LL TAKE GOOD CARE OF HER AT THE STATION.

1432
01:15:53,904 --> 01:15:55,530
HURRY UP NOW. YOU'LL BE LATE.

1433
01:15:55,864 --> 01:15:56,864
GOOD LUCK.

1434
01:16:00,452 --> 01:16:02,037
GOODBYE, MARILLA.

1435
01:16:02,537 --> 01:16:04,122
| DON'T KNOW WHAT I'D DO WITHOUT YOU.

1436
01:16:05,582 --> 01:16:07,125
YOU'VE BOTH BEEN SO WONDERFUL.

1437
01:16:07,542 --> 01:16:08,686
BUT | WON'T BE GONE FOR LONG,

1438
01:16:08,710 --> 01:16:10,462
AND | PROMISE "LL WRITE AS OFTEN ASI CAN."

1439
01:16:12,547 --> 01:16:13,547
GOODBYE.

1440
01:16:13,715 --> 01:16:21,715
(music)

1441
01:16:24,601 --> 01:16:25,601
WELL, MARILLA,

1442
01:16:25,727 --> 01:16:28,480
| NEVER WOULD HAVE BELIEVED AN ORPHACOULD TURN OUT SO FINE.

1443
01:16:29,147 --> 01:16:32,400
NO ONE COULD DENY SHE'S REAL TALL AND STYLISH NOW.

1444
01:16:32,734 --> 01:16:34,486
NOBODY AT ALL.

1445
01:16:36,738 --> 01:16:38,573
Marilla: | CAN'T HELP REMEMBERING HER.

1446
01:16:38,907 --> 01:16:40,033
AS ALITTLE GIRL.

1447
01:16:40,742 --> 01:16:42,661
AWFUL HARD | WAS BEWILDERED,

1448
01:16:43,120 --> 01:16:45,580
TRYING TO MANAGE HER.

1449
01:16:45,914 --> 01:16:47,666
MATTHEW UNDERSTOOD HER BETTER.

1450
01:16:49,251 --> 01:16:52,129
WELL, IT'S TO YOUR CREDIT YOU'VE CHANGED HER AS MUCH AS YOU DID.

1451
01:16:53,713 --> 01:16:56,508
OH, SHE HASN'T CHANGED THAT MUCH.

1452
01:16:57,092 --> 01:16:58,718
NOT REALLY.

1453
01:16:59,094 --> 01:17:02,013
IT'S US THAT'S CHANGED, RACHEL.

1454
01:17:02,305 --> 01:17:08,061
(music)

1455
01:17:08,812 --> 01:17:11,731
HOW I'VE LONGED FOR THIS MOMENT, DIANA,

1456
01:17:12,107 --> 01:17:14,359
AND NOW THAT IT'S STARING ME IN THE FACE,

1457
01:17:14,693 --> 01:17:16,903
| CAN'T BEAR THE THOUGHT OF LEAVING.

1458
01:17:17,654 --> 01:17:20,407
WE SAW GIL BLYTHE OFF TO MEDICAL SCHOOL LAST WEEK.

1459
01:17:22,826 --> 01:17:25,078
DID HE... SAY ANYTHING, DIANA?

1460
01:17:26,454 --> 01:17:28,081
| THINK HE UNDERSTANDS, ANNE.

1461
01:17:33,044 --> 01:17:41,044
(music)

1462
01:17:42,387 --> 01:17:44,764
[ Chugging of train |.

1463
01:18:01,531 --> 01:18:05,327
ANNE? ANNE SHIRLEY!

1464
01:18:05,702 --> 01:18:07,329
OH, THERE YOU ARE.

1465
01:18:07,704 --> 01:18:08,704
OH, MISS STACEY.

1466
01:18:08,788 --> 01:18:10,916
IT FEELS LIKE DECADES.

1467
01:18:11,374 --> 01:18:12,974
OH, UP ALL NIGHT ON THAT DREADFUL TRAIN,

1468
01:18:13,376 --> 01:18:14,376
YOU MUST BE EXHAUSTED.

1469
01:18:14,711 --> 01:18:17,339
OH, | FEEL BROKEN-DOWN AND GREEN AND PROVINCIAL,

1470
01:18:17,714 --> 01:18:19,341
AND ONLY

1471
01:18:19,716 --> 01:18:20,693
FOR PITY'S SAKE PLEASE TAKE ME SOMEPLACE

1472
01:18:20,717 --> 01:18:21,968
WHERE | CAN HEAR MYSELF THINK.

1473
01:18:22,427 --> 01:18:24,304
"VE GOT A CAB WAITING JUST OUTSIDE."

1474
01:18:24,638 --> 01:18:25,798
WHERE ARE YOUR LUGGA TICKETS?

1475
01:18:26,556 --> 01:18:28,350
THE DRIVER CAN TAKE CARE OF YOUR TRUNK.

1476
01:18:28,725 --> 01:18:29,702
IF YOU WEREN'T HERE, MISS STACEY,

1477
01:18:29,726 --> 01:18:33,063
| THINK | SHOULD JUST SIT DOWN AND BURST INTO TEARS.

1478
01:18:33,521 --> 01:18:35,357
WELL, | CAN'T TELL YOU

1479
01:18:35,732 --> 01:18:37,452
JUST HOW HAPPY | AM TO HAVE YOU HERE, ANNE.

1480
01:18:37,734 --> 01:18:40,534
AFTER ALL, WHY BE A MEMBER OF THE BOARD OF GOVERNORS OF AN INSTITUTION,

1481
01:18:40,737 --> 01:18:41,714
IF YOU CAN'T PULL A FEW STRINGS?

1482
01:18:41,738 --> 01:18:43,365
OH, MISS STACEY, YOU DIDN'T!

1483
01:18:43,740 --> 01:18:44,717
YES, | DID.

1484
01:18:44,741 --> 01:18:48,119
(music)

1485
01:18:48,578 --> 01:18:50,705
Anne: | INTEND TO KEEP UP WITH MY WRITING.

1486
01:18:51,248 --> 01:18:54,376
THIS QUAINT OLD TOWN WILL BE A WONDERFUL INSPIRATION.

1487
01:18:54,751 --> 01:18:56,231
WELL, | THINK YOUR YOUTH AND VITALITY

1488
01:18:56,586 --> 01:18:59,381
WILL MAKE AN ENORMOUS CONTRIBUTION TO OUR LADIES' COLLEGE.

1489
01:18:59,756 --> 01:19:02,467
AFTER ALL, YOU WERE MY PRIZE PUPIL IN AVONLEA.

1490
01:19:02,842 --> 01:19:05,262
Anne: I'M SO NERVOUS ILWON'T MEET WITH THEIR EXPECTATIONS.

1491
01:19:05,679 --> 01:19:06,719
Miss Stacey: OH, NONSENSE.

1492
01:19:06,846 --> 01:19:09,474
THEY MAY BE PRIVILEGED YOUNG LADIES FROM WEALTHY FAMILIES,

1493
01:19:09,849 --> 01:19:12,477
BUT THEY'RE SPOILED AND PAMPERED, MANY OF THEM.

1494
01:19:12,852 --> 01:19:16,481
(music)

1495
01:19:16,856 --> 01:19:19,776
GREAT JEHOSOPHAT! WHAT RICHNESS!

1496
01:19:20,277 --> 01:19:22,487
THIS IS FAR MORE GRACIOUS

1497
01:19:22,862 --> 01:19:24,614
THAN | EVER DREAMED COULD EXIST.

1498
01:19:26,700 --> 01:19:28,034
[ Rapping on door |.

1499
01:19:36,334 --> 01:19:37,654
GOOD MORNING, MAAM. GOOD MORNING.

1500
01:19:37,877 --> 01:19:39,855
COULD YOU PLEASE TELL MISS PRINGLE THAT MISS STACEY

1501
01:19:39,879 --> 01:19:43,508
AND MISS ANNE SHIRLEY ARE HERE TO SEE HER.

1502
01:19:43,883 --> 01:19:45,523
| THINK YOU'LL BE QUITE COMFORTABLE HERE.

1503
01:19:45,885 --> 01:19:47,637
MRS. TOM PRINGLE ISON THE ALUMNI.

1504
01:19:48,013 --> 01:19:50,515
SHE'S BEEN BOARDING TEACHERS FROM KINGSPORT LADIES' COLLEGE

1505
01:19:50,890 --> 01:19:51,890
FOR 30 YEARS NOW.

1506
01:19:55,312 --> 01:19:57,188
MISS STACEY, HOW DELIGHTFUL TO SEE YOU.

1507
01:19:57,731 --> 01:19:58,731
AND YOU, MRS. PRINGLE.

1508
01:19:58,898 --> 01:20:00,525
MAY | INTRODUCE YOU TO MISS ANNE SHIRLEY

1509
01:20:00,900 --> 01:20:02,220
OF AVONLEA, PRINCE EDWARD ISLAND?

1510
01:20:02,527 --> 01:20:03,528
HOW DO YOU DO?

1511
01:20:04,738 --> 01:20:06,031
SHE'S OUR NEW ENGLISH TEACHER

1512
01:20:06,364 --> 01:20:07,466
AT KINGSPORT LADIES' COLLEGE,

1513
01:20:07,490 --> 01:20:09,284
WHO YOU'LL BE BOARDING THIS YEAR.

1514
01:20:09,909 --> 01:20:11,536
SHOULD | HAVE THE CABBY BRING HER TRUNK?

1515
01:20:11,911 --> 01:20:14,539
OBVIOUSLY YOU DID NOT RECEIVE MY LETTER.

1516
01:20:14,914 --> 01:20:18,543
I'M AFRAID I'VE DECIDED NOT TO TAKE HER, MISS STACEY.

1517
01:20:18,918 --> 01:20:21,546
I'M REALLY RATHER TIRED OF BEING BOTHERED

1518
01:20:21,921 --> 01:20:23,131
BOARDING STAFF.

1519
01:20:23,423 --> 01:20:24,823
MY GIRLS ARE FINISHED, AS YOU KNOW,

1520
01:20:24,924 --> 01:20:27,177
AND | REALLY SPEND SO LITTLE TIME

1521
01:20:27,469 --> 01:20:28,553
WITH THE ALUMNI.

1522
01:20:28,928 --> 01:20:30,555
BUT MRS. PRINGLE...

1523
01:20:30,930 --> 01:20:32,557
| DO APOLOGIZE FOR THE INCONVENIENCE.

1524
01:20:32,932 --> 01:20:34,434
GOOD DAY, MISS STACEY.

1525
01:20:34,768 --> 01:20:35,768
NOT AT ALL.

1526
01:20:37,771 --> 01:20:39,564
GOOD DAY.

1527
01:20:39,939 --> 01:20:41,566
HOW TYPICALLY PRINGLE.

1528
01:20:41,941 --> 01:20:44,861
AS SMOOTH AS CREAM, EVEN WHEN THEY'RE WORKING AGAINST YOU.

1529
01:20:45,362 --> 01:20:48,698
WELL, WE SHALL SEE ABOUT THAT. HMM?

1530
01:20:51,785 --> 01:20:53,578
WHAT IS IT, MISS STACEY?

1531
01:20:53,953 --> 01:20:56,581
KINGSPORT IS FULL OF PRINGLES AND HALF-PRINGLES.

1532
01:20:56,956 --> 01:20:58,676
THEY'RE THE OLD MONEY THAT RULES THIS TOWN,

1533
01:20:58,958 --> 01:21:00,638
AND MRS. TOM PRING BOSSES THE WHOLE TRIBE.

1534
01:21:00,960 --> 01:21:02,670
| WAS AFRAID THEY'D BE DOWN ON YOU.

1535
01:21:03,046 --> 01:21:05,673
WHY SHOULD THEY BE? I'M A TOTAL STRANGER.

1536
01:21:06,049 --> 01:21:08,676
ONE OF THEIR COUSINS, MISS AMY PRINGLE BOOTHE,

1537
01:21:09,052 --> 01:21:10,678
APPLIED FOR YOUR POSITION,

1538
01:21:11,054 --> 01:21:14,682
AND WAS ABYSMALLY LESS QUALIFIED, | MIGHT ADD.

1539
01:21:15,058 --> 01:21:16,684
HOWEVER, WHEN THE BOARD ANNOUNCED

1540
01:21:17,060 --> 01:21:18,037
THAT THEY HAD ACCEPTED YOUR APPLICATION,

1541
01:21:18,061 --> 01:21:19,687
WELL THE WHOLE KIT AND KABOODLE OF THEM

1542
01:21:20,063 --> 01:21:21,689
JUST THREW BACK THEIR HEADS AND HOWLED.

1543
01:21:22,065 --> 01:21:23,983
UH, KINGSPORT LADIES' COLLEGE, PLEASE, DRIVER.

1544
01:21:24,484 --> 01:21:26,694
WELL, THEY'RE NOT GOING TO GET AWAY WITH IT.

1545
01:21:27,070 --> 01:21:28,696
THEY CAN'T BOYCOTT THE BOARD'S DECISION.

1546
01:21:29,072 --> 01:21:30,072
IT'S UNDEMOCRATIC.

1547
01:21:31,908 --> 01:21:35,245
Anne: I'M NOT SURE | QUITE ALWAYS TRUST DEMOCRACY.

1548
01:21:35,537 --> 01:21:37,897
THEY'VE ALWAYS RULED THE ROOST HERE, THE WHOLE CLAN OF THEM.

1549
01:21:38,081 --> 01:21:39,707
POLITICALLY AND SOCIALLY.

1550
01:21:40,083 --> 01:21:42,710
WELL, THEY MAY OWN THE LUMBER MILL,

1551
01:21:43,086 --> 01:21:46,714
THE RAILWAY, THE GAS WORKS AND THE WOOLEN MILL,

1552
01:21:47,090 --> 01:21:50,718
BUT | WILL NOT ALLOW THE PRINGLES TO DICTATE OUR SYSTEM OF EDUCATION.

1553
01:21:51,094 --> 01:21:52,720
YOU CANT IMAGINE HOW NERVOUS | AM NOW.

1554
01:21:53,096 --> 01:21:54,096
[ Chuckling ]

1555
01:21:54,931 --> 01:22:02,931
(music)

1556
01:22:08,194 --> 01:22:09,874
MISS KATHANE BROOKE IS THE PRINCIPAL HERE.

1557
01:22:10,196 --> 01:22:12,824
A BIT OFA MARTINET IN MATTERS OF DISCIPLINE,

1558
01:22:13,199 --> 01:22:16,828
FROM TIME TO TIME, BUT I'M SURE

1559
01:22:17,203 --> 01:22:19,181
THAT WE CAN RESOLVE WHATEVER LITTLE DIFFERENCES OF OPINION

1560
01:22:19,205 --> 01:22:20,832
THAT MIGHT ARISE.

1561
01:22:21,207 --> 01:22:29,207
(music)

1562
01:22:31,217 --> 01:22:32,635
[ Rapping on door |.

1563
01:22:33,052 --> 01:22:34,052
COME IN.

1564
01:22:34,220 --> 01:22:35,847
GOOD MORNING, MISS BROOKE.

1565
01:22:36,222 --> 01:22:38,850
MISS STACEY. PLEASE FORGIVE THE INTRUSION,

1566
01:22:39,225 --> 01:22:40,786
BUT | WAS JUST SO EAGER TO INTRODUCE YOU

1567
01:22:40,810 --> 01:22:43,146
TO OUR NEW ENGLISH PROFESSOR, MISS ANNE SHIRLEY.

1568
01:22:43,605 --> 01:22:45,982
ONE OF THE BRIGHTEST STARS OF MY ENTIRE TEACHING CAREER.

1569
01:22:46,399 --> 01:22:48,860
SHE HAS RECENTLY PUBLISHED A SHORT WORK OF FICTION AS WELL.

1570
01:22:49,235 --> 01:22:51,863
WELCOME TO KINGSPORT, MISS SHIRLEY.

1571
01:22:52,238 --> 01:22:53,364
PLEASE SIT DOWN.

1572
01:22:53,865 --> 01:22:57,368
THANK YOU. I'M VERY PLEASED TO BE HERE.

1573
01:22:57,911 --> 01:23:00,872
MISS STACEY HAS RECOMMENDED YOU SO HIGHLY TO US.

1574
01:23:01,247 --> 01:23:03,958
| HADN'T EXPECTED ONE SO ACCOMPLISHED

1575
01:23:04,334 --> 01:23:05,334
TO BE SO YOUNG...

1576
01:23:06,169 --> 01:23:09,130
A FAULT WHICH TIME WILL CURE ALL TOO SOON.

1577
01:23:09,631 --> 01:23:12,133
MISS BROOKE, THERE SEEMS TO BE SOME SORT OF MIX-UP

1578
01:23:12,634 --> 01:23:14,385
REGARDING MISS SHIRLEY'S ACCOMMODATIONS,

1579
01:23:14,844 --> 01:23:16,322
BUT | WAS SURE THAT YOU WOULDN'T OBJECT

1580
01:23:16,346 --> 01:23:17,972
HAVING HER STAY HERE AT THE SCHOOL

1581
01:23:18,348 --> 01:23:19,974
WITH YOUR OUT-OF-TOWN BOARDING STUDENTS.

1582
01:23:20,350 --> 01:23:22,977
I'M SURE YOU'LL FIND HER TO BE THE PERFECT DEN-MOTHER FOR THEM.

1583
01:23:23,353 --> 01:23:24,979
WE HAVE NO NEED OF MATERNAL AFFECTATIONS

1584
01:23:25,355 --> 01:23:26,981
IN THIS INSTITUTE, MISS STACEY.

1585
01:23:27,357 --> 01:23:30,068
WE GOVERN BY RULES AND REGULATIONS.

1586
01:23:30,401 --> 01:23:32,987
WHICH DO REQUIRE A LEAVEN IN THE LUMP

1587
01:23:33,363 --> 01:23:34,906
FROM TIME TO TIME, MS BROOKE.

1588
01:23:35,240 --> 01:23:37,992
SHALL WE HAVE THE GROUNDSMAN BRING IN MISS SHIRLEY"S THINGS?

1589
01:23:38,368 --> 01:23:39,994
"LL HAVE THE MAID PREPARE HER ROOM."

1590
01:23:40,370 --> 01:23:42,121
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

1591
01:23:46,209 --> 01:23:49,003
SHE IS AN ABSOLUTE SERGEANT-MAJOR, MISS STACEY.

1592
01:23:49,379 --> 01:23:51,005
HOW SHALL I EVER TOLERATE HER SARCASM?

1593
01:23:51,381 --> 01:23:54,008
NONETHELESS SHE IS A DEDICATED TEACHER,

1594
01:23:54,384 --> 01:23:57,136
IF SOMEWHAT OF AN EXCES-SIVE DISCIPLINARIAN.

1595
01:23:58,304 --> 01:23:59,556
YOU JUST KEEP YOUR CHIN UP,

1596
01:23:59,931 --> 01:24:01,516
AND YOU GIVE IT YOUR VERY BEST,

1597
01:24:01,891 --> 01:24:03,768
IF ONLY TO SPITE THEM ALL.

1598
01:24:04,561 --> 01:24:06,813
YOU KNOW HOW HIGHLY | REGARD YOUR ABILITIES, ANNE.

1599
01:24:07,522 --> 01:24:09,315
| SHALL DO VERY BEST TO RISE TO THE OCCASION.

1600
01:24:09,607 --> 01:24:11,317
GOOD GIRL.

1601
01:24:11,609 --> 01:24:13,319
NOW YOU WANT TO GET YOURSELF ORGANIZED

1602
01:24:13,611 --> 01:24:15,280
BEFORE THE START OF CLASSES TOMORROW.

1603
01:24:15,613 --> 01:24:17,323
OH, HO-HO!

1604
01:24:17,615 --> 01:24:19,325
OH. THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING, MISS STACEY.

1605
01:24:19,617 --> 01:24:21,494
WE CAN DO THE REST OF OUR CATCHING UP LATER.

1606
01:24:25,331 --> 01:24:33,331
(music)

1607
01:24:56,863 --> 01:24:59,157
IN FUTURE, MISS SHIRLEY, YOU WILL KINDLY REMEMBER

1608
01:24:59,657 --> 01:25:01,701
THAT YOU ARE NOT AT LIBERTY TO MAKE ANY CHANGES,

1609
01:25:01,993 --> 01:25:04,871
NO MATTER HOW MINOR, TO THE CONVENTIONS OF THIS INSTITUTION.

1610
01:25:06,956 --> 01:25:07,956
/M SORRY, I...

1611
01:25:07,999 --> 01:25:09,879
| WAS JUST SO MOVED BY YOUR INSPIRING QUOTATION,

1612
01:25:10,001 --> 01:25:11,711
|IWANTED TO EMBELLISH IT.

1613
01:25:12,003 --> 01:25:14,714
DON'T PATRONIZE ME.

