01:51:27,160 --> 01:51:29,454
benefit concert?

2084
01:51:30,163 --> 01:51:34,250
Highlighting a play perhaps directed by Miss Anne Shirley...

2085
01:51:34,626 --> 01:51:38,254
It will have to be something with a number of superb roles

2086
01:51:38,588 --> 01:51:39,565
in it though.

2087
01:51:39,589 --> 01:51:42,050
And strong dramatic content.

2088
01:51:42,342 --> 01:51:44,382
The audience will have to be completely overwhelmed.

2089
01:51:44,594 --> 01:51:46,572
| think every Pringle parent would gladly pay to see their

2090
01:51:46,596 --> 01:51:50,266
daughter's names in the program, don't you think!

2091
01:51:50,600 --> 01:51:55,313
Let's see uh, 100 tickets at $25 a ticket why that makes

2092
01:51:55,647 --> 01:52:01,277
exactly $2500...

2093
01:52:01,611 --> 01:52:03,279
That's an outrageous price!

2094
01:52:03,613 --> 01:52:05,493
Do you honestly think anyone would pay for that?

2095
01:52:05,824 --> 01:52:10,286
Yes, and all the money will go directly to the school.

2096
01:52:10,620 --> 01:52:15,375
You are perfectly ingenious Miss Stacey.

2097
01:52:15,750 --> 01:52:18,294
We'll show the Pringles the meaning

2098
01:52:18,628 --> 01:52:21,297
of the word "capitalism".

2099
01:52:21,631 --> 01:52:25,677
Justa minute Anne, | think that you should have

2100
01:52:26,219 --> 01:52:27,339
a look at these old diaries.

2101
01:52:27,637 --> 01:52:29,917
Mrs. Stanton, our librarian, and | are preparing a history

2102
01:52:30,432 --> 01:52:31,617
of Kingsport and we literally stumbled across

2103
01:52:31,641 --> 01:52:33,309
those in the archives.

2104
01:52:33,643 --> 01:52:35,729
They were written by Captain Abraham Pringle

2105
01:52:36,271 --> 01:52:39,482
the founder of Kingsport.

2106
01:52:41,568 --> 01:52:45,321
My dear Anne, if you want to win the game

2107
01:52:45,613 --> 01:52:48,408
you have to understand the players.

2108
01:52:48,742 --> 01:52:51,411
"| see.

2109
01:52:51,745 --> 01:52:56,374
"And so, for the last time the old teacher passed by the cruel

2110
01:52:56,666 --> 01:53:01,212
portrait of herself etched in the wall by her former students.

2111
01:53:01,588 --> 01:53:04,424
Gertrude glimpsed the old woman's haughty loneliness

2112
01:53:04,758 --> 01:53:07,427
as she retreated silently into the garden.

2113
01:53:07,761 --> 01:53:09,739
Shortly thereafter they learned that the hand of death

2114
01:53:09,763 --> 01:53:12,056
had touched her.

2115
01:53:12,557 --> 01:53:14,744
And Gertrude was haunted by the realization that she could

2116
01:53:14,768 --> 01:53:19,439
never thank the woman who had silently given her so much.

2117
01:53:19,773 --> 01:53:23,526
It was more than she could bear".

2118
01:53:25,612 --> 01:53:27,757
At this point in the term | would like to dedicate this

2119
01:53:27,781 --> 01:53:29,908
short story to each of you young ladies who have made

2120
01:53:30,450 --> 01:53:34,370
the first few weeks here for me so meaningful.

2121
01:53:34,662 --> 01:53:37,957
Class dismissed.

2122
01:53:39,375 --> 01:53:40,655
What are these girls crying for?

2123
01:53:40,835 --> 01:53:43,588
I've been reading them a short story, Miss Brooke.

2124
01:53:46,674 --> 01:53:52,514
Good grief - crying over an English lesson!

2125
01:53:52,847 --> 01:53:55,433
Miss Brooke is here to discuss my suggestion of a play

2126
01:53:55,809 --> 01:53:56,809
and benefit concert.

2127
01:53:56,851 --> 01:53:59,521
| think it's scandalous, but my opinion matters little

2128
01:53:59,854 --> 01:54:03,358
since the school needs the funds.

2129
01:54:03,691 --> 01:54:05,401
Exactly.

2130
01:54:05,693 --> 01:54:08,530
| was hoping you would assist me in the coaching, Miss Brooke.

2131
01:54:08,863 --> 01:54:10,240
| don't know why you would.

2132
01:54:10,532 --> 01:54:11,842
Since | had nothing to do with drawing up

2133
01:54:11,866 --> 01:54:13,535
this ridiculous scheme!

2134
01:54:13,868 --> 01:54:16,538
The most important question is, then, who shall play the leading

2135
01:54:16,871 --> 01:54:18,540
role of Mary Queen of Scots?

2136
01:54:18,873 --> 01:54:20,851
| think - We don't want any green horn in the role.

2137
01:54:20,875 --> 01:54:22,595
I'm not going to be associated with anything

2138
01:54:22,752 --> 01:54:23,752
that isn't successful.

2139
01:54:23,878 --> 01:54:25,856
Jen Pringle is the only one! Can think of who could

2140
01:54:25,880 --> 01:54:27,549
play the part.

2141
01:54:27,882 --> 01:54:31,886
No one else has the necessary personality.

2142
01:54:32,428 --> 01:54:36,641
| can't deny that Jen has a natural flair for acting.

2143
01:54:36,975 --> 01:54:38,560
Then it's all settled.

2144
01:54:38,935 --> 01:54:40,955
Why, | think Miss Brooke will make an excellent coach.

2145
01:54:40,979 --> 01:54:42,957
And Miss MacKay and Miss Kerr can do the decorations

2146
01:54:42,981 --> 01:54:46,651
and I'll see to the hiring of the hall and the band.

2147
01:54:46,985 --> 01:54:49,654
Perhaps | can even entice a famous soprano from Fredericton

2148
01:54:49,988 --> 01:54:51,656
to sing between acts at no charge!

2149
01:54:51,990 --> 01:54:53,658
| trust she'll sing for the creditors

2150
01:54:53,992 --> 01:54:55,451
if the whole thing flops!

2151
01:54:55,743 --> 01:54:58,288
But, don't say | didn't warn you!

2152
01:55:08,464 --> 01:55:11,801
Make your brush stroke move like furious fire, furiously.

2153
01:55:12,594 --> 01:55:16,764
Shoot out!

2154
01:55:18,808 --> 01:55:20,602
Make great big stitches so they won't show.

2155
01:55:20,977 --> 01:55:21,871
| implore you!

2156
01:55:21,895 --> 01:55:22,997
Don't just stand there like limp rags...

2157
01:55:23,021 --> 01:55:23,831
Help me, help me.

2158
01:55:23,855 --> 01:55:24,855
Feel it, feel it!

2159
01:55:25,023 --> 01:55:26,000
Let go the Queen.

2160
01:55:26,024 --> 01:55:27,525
Myra, you're using you upstage hand.

2161
01:55:27,859 --> 01:55:29,694
You're hiding your face.

2162
01:55:30,028 --> 01:55:33,156
Help me my mistress, have mercy.

2163
01:55:34,449 --> 01:55:38,286
Mercy nay | am innocent.

2164
01:55:39,454 --> 01:55:42,415
Save me sweet lady.

2165
01:55:42,707 --> 01:55:45,418
Will ye slay save me too?

2166
01:55:45,710 --> 01:55:48,838
Drag him away, pluck his hands off her.

2167
01:55:49,339 --> 01:55:50,459
This scene looks ridiculous.

2168
01:55:50,715 --> 01:55:53,051
Lam not gonna lower myself any further.

2169
01:55:53,593 --> 01:55:54,695
Hattie youre as stiff as a poker!

2170
01:55:54,719 --> 01:55:56,429
| can't help it.

2171
01:55:56,721 --> 01:55:57,698
| don't want to bruise myself.

2172
01:55:57,722 --> 01:56:01,267
If |can go down easily, | will.

2173
01:56:01,559 --> 01:56:03,436
You've all seen Essie carrying on.

2174
01:56:03,728 --> 01:56:06,439
Now do it this way.

2175
01:56:06,731 --> 01:56:10,443
Lam innocent, Save me sweet lady.

2176
01:56:10,735 --> 01:56:12,445
Oh!

2177
01:56:12,737 --> 01:56:14,537
..now the Queen she orders the guards to halt.

2178
01:56:14,739 --> 01:56:17,408
But the guards drag Rizzio away.

2179
01:56:18,993 --> 01:56:20,912
Now Hattie, you try it.

2180
01:56:22,997 --> 01:56:28,836
Lam innocent, save me sweet lady uh huh, uh huh.

2181
01:56:29,170 --> 01:56:31,839
| refuse to play opposite her.

2182
01:56:32,173 --> 01:56:34,151
Well, she is the only one who can be remotely convincing

2183
01:56:34,175 --> 01:56:37,011
as an Italian musician.

2184
01:56:38,096 --> 01:56:39,931
Do what you can Miss Brooke.

2185
01:56:40,264 --> 01:56:42,016
Well, don't blame me if the audience leaves.

2186
01:56:45,103 --> 01:56:49,023
Once more Hattie, and please relax!

2187
01:56:52,735 --> 01:56:54,570
Emmeline!

2188
01:56:54,904 --> 01:56:55,881
Emmeline!

2189
01:56:55,905 --> 01:56:58,241
What is it, what ts it?

2190
01:57:02,704 --> 01:57:04,789
We've missed having you in our play.

2191
01:57:06,165 --> 01:57:09,377
Oh, I'm so sorry about what happened with your father.

2192
01:57:09,711 --> 01:57:11,689
Once everything's calmed down I'm hoping | can get a chance

2193
01:57:11,713 --> 01:57:15,383
to speak with him and try to explain.

2194
01:57:15,717 --> 01:57:17,176
He isn't here.

2195
01:57:17,552 --> 01:57:19,762
He's gone back to Boston.

2196
01:57:20,263 --> 01:57:23,433
Oh, Miss Shirley, I've always wanted to do a play...

2197
01:57:23,766 --> 01:57:27,395
I've never had much of a chance to do anything.

2198
01:57:27,729 --> 01:57:31,399
Papa will never let me come back to this school.

2199
01:57:31,733 --> 01:57:34,402
Lam to spend the rest of the year with grandmama, alone.

2200
01:57:34,736 --> 01:57:38,364
Oh Emmeline...

2201
01:57:39,240 --> 01:57:41,075
Perhaps | can get another copy of the play.

2202
01:57:41,409 --> 01:57:44,078
I'll coach you at home, if you like.

2203
01:57:44,412 --> 01:57:46,132
I'm sure your father will let you come back

2204
01:57:46,414 --> 01:57:48,082
to college next term.

2205
01:57:48,416 --> 01:57:49,393
| don't think so.

2206
01:57:49,417 --> 01:57:51,169
| don't think grandmama will either.

2207
01:57:51,711 --> 01:57:55,173
| had to sneak out while she and Aunt Pauline were napping.

2208
01:57:58,259 --> 01:58:01,095
Is someone helping you along with your studies?

2209
01:58:01,429 --> 01:58:04,682
You don't want to fall behind.

2210
01:58:06,267 --> 01:58:10,521
Well, then | shall have to have a chat with your Grandmama.

2211
01:58:11,022 --> 01:58:14,108
Will you?

2212
01:58:14,442 --> 01:58:16,110
You should hurry along home.

2213
01:58:16,444 --> 01:58:17,987
You don't want to get her cross.

2214
01:58:18,321 --> 01:58:20,114
And | promise | will come by tomorrow

2215
01:58:20,448 --> 01:58:23,201
and | will speak with her.

2216
01:58:26,287 --> 01:58:28,122
Oh, it's number 10 Mapple Terrace.

2217
01:58:28,456 --> 01:58:29,433
You won't forget...

2218
01:58:29,457 --> 01:58:31,125
Of course not.

2219
01:58:31,459 --> 01:58:33,211
Off you go.

2220
01:59:07,411 --> 01:59:08,411
Yes?

2221
01:59:08,663 --> 01:59:10,263
| should like to speak with Mrs. Harris.

2222
01:59:10,581 --> 01:59:11,558
My name is - You can't.

2223
01:59:11,582 --> 01:59:13,251
She is ill and won't be disturbed.

2224
01:59:13,584 --> 01:59:14,561
Good day.

2225
01:59:14,585 --> 01:59:17,255
May | speak with Emmeline Harris, then?

2226
01:59:17,588 --> 01:59:20,341
She isn't allowed to have visitors.

2227
01:59:20,675 --> 01:59:24,262
Is Captain Harris coming back to - Lives in Boston miss.

2228
01:59:24,595 --> 01:59:26,264
Seldom visits here.

2229
01:59:26,597 --> 01:59:31,269
Could you tell Emmeline that Anne Shirley came to see her?

2230
01:59:31,602 --> 01:59:33,688
Thank you.

2231
02:00:00,464 --> 02:00:06,888
My Dear Mrs. Harris: | thought you might be interested in these

2232
02:00:07,471 --> 02:00:11,309
diaries belonging to Captain Abraham Pringle, which | found

2233
02:00:11,642 --> 02:00:14,312
in the City Archives.

2234
02:00:14,645 --> 02:00:17,315
There are some wonderful tributes in here by Captain.

2235
02:00:17,648 --> 02:00:21,319
Pringle to your late husband, Captain Harris.

2236
02:00:21,652 --> 02:00:24,322
| hope you enjoy reading them as much as | did.

2237
02:00:24,655 --> 02:00:29,202
Sincerely, Anne Shirley, Kingsport Ladies College.

2238
02:00:32,496 --> 02:00:37,126
| have a delivery for Miss Shirley.

2239
02:00:37,585 --> 02:00:38,061
Well you're in luck.

2240
02:00:38,085 --> 02:00:39,503
Lam Miss Shirley.

2241
02:00:40,588 --> 02:00:42,506
Thank you.

2242
02:00:56,103 --> 02:00:59,523
So then it's tomorrow at noon ts it Mrs. Harris...

2243
02:01:23,631 --> 02:01:26,467
Miss Shirley Madam.

2244
02:01:27,635 --> 02:01:29,470
Mama.

2245
02:01:29,804 --> 02:01:31,597
Mama...

2246
02:01:32,139 --> 02:01:34,558
Good grief girl youre aggravating!

2247
02:01:34,976 --> 02:01:37,561
Miss Shirley.

2248
02:01:37,895 --> 02:01:38,872
What?

2249
02:01:38,896 --> 02:01:41,649
Miss Shirley!

2250
02:01:45,486 --> 02:01:48,656
Saints alive, why didn't you say so in the first place?

2251
02:01:51,742 --> 02:01:55,454
So, this is the infamous Miss Shirley.

2252
02:01:55,788 --> 02:01:58,582
Come to take her pound of flesh...

2253
02:01:58,916 --> 02:02:00,876
How do you do Mrs. Harris?

2254
02:02:01,377 --> 02:02:04,588
Far from well.

2255
02:02:04,922 --> 02:02:08,592
How much do you want for these diaries?

2256
02:02:08,926 --> 02:02:11,679
| hadn't any Intention of selling them.

2257
02:02:13,764 --> 02:02:17,601
Is there any use in asking you to sit down?

2258
02:02:17,935 --> 02:02:19,520
Yes

2259
02:02:19,895 --> 02:02:21,605
thank you.

2260
02:02:21,939 --> 02:02:25,609
Who else has seen these?

2261
02:02:25,943 --> 02:02:29,488
No one as far as | know.

2262
02:02:29,822 --> 02:02:32,658
Then I'm ready to negotiate.

2263
02:02:32,992 --> 02:02:38,706
| will give you what you want if you give me your word not

2264
02:02:38,998 --> 02:02:45,796
to reveal this monstrosity to the rest of the Pringles.

2265
02:02:46,088 --> 02:02:48,716
| was only hoping | might convince you to let me tutor

2266
02:02:49,050 --> 02:02:50,770
your granddaughter Emmeline as | understand

2267
02:02:51,052 --> 02:02:53,721
that she will not be returning to school.

2268
02:02:54,055 --> 02:02:56,640
Oh clever aren't we?

2269
02:02:57,016 --> 02:02:59,727
Sugarcoated blackmail!

2270
02:03:00,061 --> 02:03:05,733
You want a regular salary to keep you quiet, is that it?

2271
02:03:06,067 --> 02:03:08,736
| beg your pardon?

2272
02:03:09,070 --> 02:03:12,740
Innocent as doves, cunning as serpents.

2273
02:03:13,074 --> 02:03:15,743
You knew when you found that scandalous entry

2274
02:03:16,077 --> 02:03:17,745
about my husband it wasn't true.

2275
02:03:18,079 --> 02:03:19,747
| couldn't be true!

2276
02:03:20,081 --> 02:03:21,801
The rest of the Pringles will be dee-lighted

2277
02:03:22,083 --> 02:03:23,250
to believe it won't they?

2278
02:03:23,918 --> 02:03:27,838
And make us the laughing stock of Kingsport!

2279
02:03:28,339 --> 02:03:30,758
Which scandalous entry?

2280
02:03:31,092 --> 02:03:34,762
Oh, so there's more than one, is there?

2281
02:03:35,096 --> 02:03:36,847
Pauline.

2282
02:03:46,023 --> 02:03:50,861
Josiah Harris' ship was burned and their boats taken.

2283
02:03:51,195 --> 02:03:53,864
Harris and the crew nearly starved.

2284
02:03:54,198 --> 02:04:02,198
In the end they They ate Jonas Selkirk who had shot himself

2285
02:04:04,208 --> 02:04:07,878
they lived on him until rescued.

2286
02:04:08,212 --> 02:04:09,880
Harris told me himself.

2287
02:04:10,214 --> 02:04:14,969
Seemed to think it was a good joke.

2288
02:04:16,053 --> 02:04:18,889
On occasion papa would get so angry he'd...

2289
02:04:19,223 --> 02:04:20,307
Pauline!

2290
02:04:21,016 --> 02:04:22,016
Be quiet!

2291
02:04:22,226 --> 02:04:23,894
That is a lie.

2292
02:04:24,228 --> 02:04:26,897
My husband never ate anyone dead or alive.

2293
02:04:27,231 --> 02:04:29,900
Let alone Jonas Selkirk.

2294
02:04:30,234 --> 02:04:31,902
Abraham Pringle wrote that nonsense

2295
02:04:32,236 --> 02:04:34,905
to get a rise out of his silly wife.

2296
02:04:35,239 --> 02:04:38,993
Amy Pringle was notoriously gullible.

2297
02:04:39,326 --> 02:04:42,997
Oh, please Miss Shirley, don't show these to anyone.

2298
02:04:43,330 --> 02:04:45,082
Our Pringle relations might publicize it.

2299
02:04:45,458 --> 02:04:47,001
We'll do anything!

2300
02:04:47,334 --> 02:04:49,003
Ow.

2301
02:04:49,336 --> 02:04:50,336
Now Miss Shirley.

2302
02:04:50,463 --> 02:04:56,010
How much do you want to 'tutor my granddaughter?

2303
02:04:56,343 --> 02:04:58,971
Oh you've misunderstood me completely.

2304
02:04:59,305 --> 02:05:01,015
I'm not threatening you!

2305
02:05:01,348 --> 02:05:03,326
| just thought you'd enjoy all the other splendid things

2306
02:05:03,350 --> 02:05:05,227
said about your husband.

2307
02:05:05,728 --> 02:05:08,230
| never dreamed of telling anyone he was a cannibal.

2308
02:05:12,026 --> 02:05:18,073
Well naturally we tend to be a little suspicious of strangers

2309
02:05:18,449 --> 02:05:24,079
in Kingsport, perhaps we have misjudged you.

2310
02:05:24,413 --> 02:05:28,667
| suppose the child should continue with her studies.

2311
02:05:29,168 --> 02:05:30,168
Pauline has no time.

2312
02:05:30,419 --> 02:05:35,090
She's busy looking after me.

2313
02:05:35,424 --> 02:05:38,177
You won't mention this misunderstanding

2314
02:05:38,552 --> 02:05:40,179
to anyone will you?

2315
02:05:40,513 --> 02:05:46,185
I'll try to remember not to...

2316
02:05:46,560 --> 02:05:50,189
And when do you want to start?

2317
02:05:50,523 --> 02:05:52,191
Immediately.

2318
02:05:52,525 --> 02:05:55,194
Oh.

2319
02:05:55,569 --> 02:05:57,547
If two angles in a triangle are equal to each other, the two

2320
02:05:57,571 --> 02:06:01,492
sides opposite these two angles are equal to each other.

2321
02:06:02,868 --> 02:06:05,704
Emmeline, why hasn't anyone replaced your spectacles?

2322
02:06:06,038 --> 02:06:08,415
Well, papa says | don't really need to wear them

2323
02:06:08,874 --> 02:06:09,874
as much as | do.

2324
02:06:10,084 --> 02:06:13,003
And Grandmama won't because she's an old skin-flint!

2325
02:06:14,255 --> 02:06:15,255
Who gave you those, then?

2326
02:06:15,506 --> 02:06:19,176
Mother Superior at the convent in Boston two years ago.

2327
02:06:19,510 --> 02:06:22,137
Anyway, I'm only supposed to use them for reading.

2328
02:06:22,429 --> 02:06:23,490
You simply cannot use them anymore.

2329
02:06:23,514 --> 02:06:26,392
You must have another pair!

2330
02:06:31,855 --> 02:06:36,402
| found another copy Mary queen of Scots!

2331
02:06:36,735 --> 02:06:40,155
Oh, her very name just thrills me to my fingertips!

2332
02:06:40,489 --> 02:06:42,529
| don't believe she really murdered Darnley, do you?

2333
02:06:42,825 --> 02:06:44,493
Shh!

2334
02:06:44,827 --> 02:06:48,414
Heaven help you if you wake her up!

2335
02:06:48,747 --> 02:06:51,041
| think it's ever so dramatic, don't you?

2336
02:06:51,542 --> 02:06:53,502
It's a very challenging role.

2337
02:06:53,836 --> 02:06:56,505
We used to have dramatics and music at the convent.

2338
02:06:56,839 --> 02:06:59,508
