And don't sit in a draft either.

2594
02:20:35,323 --> 02:20:38,076
And don"t slide down the banisters.

2595
02:20:38,410 --> 02:20:39,410
Mama!

2596
02:20:39,911 --> 02:20:41,389
Well you did at Nancy Pringle's wedding.

2597
02:20:41,413 --> 02:20:43,998
Mama, that was 25 years ago.

2598
02:20:44,332 --> 02:20:45,332
What do you think | am?

2599
02:20:45,417 --> 02:20:46,394
Go on girl.

2600
02:20:46,418 --> 02:20:48,086
Don't stand there jabbering.

2601
02:20:48,420 --> 02:20:50,088
Do you want to miss your train?

2602
02:20:50,422 --> 02:20:52,215
No, Mama.

2603
02:20:52,590 --> 02:20:54,634
And if I'm not here when you come back, remember,

2604
02:20:55,009 --> 02:20:56,249
lay me out in my wedding dress.

2605
02:20:56,302 --> 02:20:58,012
And mind my hair is crimped!

2606
02:20:58,304 --> 02:21:00,432
| don't know how you'll manage her Miss Shirley.

2607
02:21:00,849 --> 02:21:03,101
She's such a baby.

2608
02:21:08,982 --> 02:21:12,527
| never thought I'd ever get a chance to visit Maplehurst.

2609
02:21:19,075 --> 02:21:21,828
Ettie, Ettie Pringle get away from there,

2610
02:21:22,120 --> 02:21:24,831
that's Mrs. Harris' carriage.

2611
02:21:25,123 --> 02:21:26,100
This is outrageous.

2612
02:21:26,124 --> 02:21:27,834
| haven't been outside...

2613
02:21:28,126 --> 02:21:30,670
If | catch cold girl, | Shall hold you responsible.

2614
02:21:31,087 --> 02:21:32,087
Nonsense!

2615
02:21:32,130 --> 02:21:33,465
| want you to enjoy the sunshine

2616
02:21:33,965 --> 02:21:35,842
and all the beautiful autumn colours.

2617
02:21:36,217 --> 02:21:38,154
We'll have a lovely carriage ride and you can criticize

2618
02:21:38,178 --> 02:21:39,929
everyone we pass by!

2619
02:21:40,221 --> 02:21:41,931
Criticize?

2620
02:21:42,223 --> 02:21:44,934
That's a very strange idea Miss Shirley.

2621
02:21:45,226 --> 02:21:46,936
That's not Christian.

2622
02:21:47,228 --> 02:21:49,063
It's simply not Christian.

2623
02:21:50,440 --> 02:21:51,560
What is the meaning of this!

2624
02:21:51,774 --> 02:21:55,236
Miss Shirley, | won't stand for anymore of your monkeyshines!

2625
02:21:55,570 --> 02:21:57,906
You have such handsome Carriages and never use them.

2626
02:21:58,239 --> 02:21:59,491
You put them back do you hear!

2627
02:22:00,033 --> 02:22:02,160
They've not been out for seven years!

2628
02:22:02,494 --> 02:22:04,494
All the more reason to bring them out and use them.

2629
02:22:04,579 --> 02:22:06,247
Stop being so selfish.

2630
02:22:06,581 --> 02:22:08,166
Good morning girls.

2631
02:22:08,500 --> 02:22:09,584
You look lovely!

2632
02:22:10,126 --> 02:22:11,061
You bring me back in!

2633
02:22:11,085 --> 02:22:12,062
Do you hear?

2634
02:22:12,086 --> 02:22:13,254
This is anarchy!

2635
02:22:13,588 --> 02:22:17,383
Who are these rabble-rousers?

2636
02:22:18,468 --> 02:22:21,054
Oh dear saints above | shall swoon.

2637
02:22:21,471 --> 02:22:23,264
| can't stand all this fresh air.

2638
02:22:23,598 --> 02:22:25,892
It's such a pretty day, | thought you could host

2639
02:22:26,351 --> 02:22:27,351
a picnic for the school.

2640
02:22:27,602 --> 02:22:30,271
| don't eat my lunch outside with anyone girl.

2641
02:22:30,605 --> 02:22:32,273
I'm not a raggle-taggle gypsy.

2642
02:22:32,607 --> 02:22:33,584
Take me in! Take me in!

2643
02:22:33,608 --> 02:22:36,736
Hush now, Mrs. Harris; Some of these young girls are Pringles.

2644
02:22:37,237 --> 02:22:38,214
Pringles?

2645
02:22:38,238 --> 02:22:39,364
Yes.

2646
02:22:39,697 --> 02:22:41,675
And you don't want them running home and telling tales.

2647
02:22:41,699 --> 02:22:43,368
You'll pay for this.

2648
02:22:43,701 --> 02:22:46,371
If | catch a chill...

2649
02:22:46,704 --> 02:22:48,182
You said you wanted a day off from your

2650
02:22:48,206 --> 02:22:48,849
wheelchair anyway Grandmama.

2651
02:22:48,873 --> 02:22:49,958
Be quiet!

2652
02:22:54,128 --> 02:22:55,964
Good morning Mrs. Harris.

2653
02:22:56,297 --> 02:22:58,967
You look awfully chipper.

2654
02:22:59,300 --> 02:23:00,969
Thank you Alec McGuinness.

2655
02:23:01,302 --> 02:23:02,971
Thank you.

2656
02:23:03,304 --> 02:23:05,181
Well, what does it matter if | die anyway?

2657
02:23:05,473 --> 02:23:10,061
I've been living on borrowed time for too long as it is.

2658
02:23:34,627 --> 02:23:37,422
Such friendly people!

2659
02:23:37,755 --> 02:23:39,507
Charming neighbours.

2660
02:23:39,841 --> 02:23:43,636
You know | don't approve of your criticizing people my dear.

2661
02:23:43,970 --> 02:23:48,516
May | ask is that all your own hair.

2662
02:23:48,850 --> 02:23:49,827
Yes.

2663
02:23:49,851 --> 02:23:51,352
Every bit.

2664
02:23:51,728 --> 02:23:52,728
Pity it's red.

2665
02:23:53,229 --> 02:23:56,524
But | believe red is becoming quite popular again.

2666
02:23:56,858 --> 02:23:58,610
Thank you.

2667
02:24:36,022 --> 02:24:37,607
And another one?

2668
02:24:37,940 --> 02:24:39,609
How delightful!

2669
02:24:39,942 --> 02:24:41,611
Now, thank you my dear.

2670
02:24:41,944 --> 02:24:45,698
This is my gift to you, Emmeline.

2671
02:24:48,159 --> 02:24:50,286
Oh, Miss Shirley!

2672
02:24:50,828 --> 02:24:52,622
However did you pay for this?

2673
02:24:52,955 --> 02:24:54,749
| had some lucky savings put aside.

2674
02:24:57,335 --> 02:24:58,335
Oh!

2675
02:24:58,378 --> 02:25:00,254
Thank you a million times over!

2676
02:25:00,963 --> 02:25:03,758
Some day I'll make it up to you!

2677
02:25:07,845 --> 02:25:10,765
Now wasn't that sweet of all these girls to give me gifts?

2678
02:25:11,140 --> 02:25:14,644
Yes, it was.

2679
02:25:14,977 --> 02:25:16,538
Yes, | rather like your laugh Miss Shirley.

2680
02:25:16,562 --> 02:25:19,774
That nervous giggle of Pauline's it gets on my nerves.

2681
02:25:21,859 --> 02:25:24,654
Well, | hope she has a wonderful time at the party.

2682
02:25:24,987 --> 02:25:26,827
She's probably over eaten and made herself ill.

2683
02:25:27,031 --> 02:25:29,659
Like her father, that girl.

2684
02:25:29,992 --> 02:25:32,745
Course, he never knew when he'd had enough.

2685
02:25:33,871 --> 02:25:38,751
Did | ever show you Josiah's picture, Miss Shirley?

2686
02:25:39,085 --> 02:25:40,837
He was very handsome.

2687
02:25:41,921 --> 02:25:44,757
Full of heroic spirit, I'd say.

2688
02:25:45,091 --> 02:25:46,068
Yes.

2689
02:25:46,092 --> 02:25:49,762
He was the handsomest man in Kingsport.

2690
02:25:50,096 --> 02:25:51,723
And he adored me.

2691
02:25:52,098 --> 02:25:54,138
We consulted each other about absolutely everything.

2692
02:25:54,267 --> 02:25:57,228
Mind you, we didn't always agree - no.

2693
02:25:58,438 --> 02:26:00,022
He had his fits of temper.

2694
02:26:00,440 --> 02:26:03,025
Oh yes, and so did I.

2695
02:26:07,947 --> 02:26:12,785
You know what he did when | bought a day-cap he didn't like?

2696
02:26:13,119 --> 02:26:14,912
| can't imagine...

2697
02:26:15,413 --> 02:26:16,873
He ate It!

2698
02:26:17,999 --> 02:26:19,333
Gave him a terrible stomach pain!

2699
02:26:19,625 --> 02:26:20,793
Yes, served him right.

2700
02:26:21,127 --> 02:26:24,922
He was so irked that | had neglected to consult him!

2701
02:26:32,013 --> 02:26:35,933
How could he go away and leave me alone and crippled like this?

2702
02:26:37,018 --> 02:26:40,730
Dying was the only thing he ever dared do without consulting me.

2703
02:26:44,066 --> 02:26:46,527
Well, it won't be long before we're together again.

2704
02:26:48,070 --> 02:26:54,994
There's no one... no man... like him... nowhere... no.

2705
02:26:55,912 --> 02:26:59,207
This is a degenerate age, Miss Shirley.

2706
02:27:01,542 --> 02:27:03,461
What about your son?

2707
02:27:05,129 --> 02:27:06,129
Morgan.

2708
02:27:07,131 --> 02:27:09,926
Oh, well he managed his money successfully

2709
02:27:10,259 --> 02:27:11,928
if that's any merit.

2710
02:27:12,261 --> 02:27:14,931
His father spoiled him.

2711
02:27:15,264 --> 02:27:18,059
No, he should never have married his cousin.

2712
02:27:19,101 --> 02:27:24,148
It was a blessing that poor Adelaide Pringle died dear soul;

2713
02:27:24,649 --> 02:27:28,069
Morgan got what he deserved | suppose.

2714
02:27:29,153 --> 02:27:32,949
That's a very inhuman attitude for a mother, Mrs. Harris.

2715
02:27:33,282 --> 02:27:36,953
Yes, well we're not exactly famous for compassion.

2716
02:27:37,286 --> 02:27:41,165
Miss Shirley, especially among ourselves.

2717
02:27:42,208 --> 02:27:44,252
Anyway they're all waiting for me to die

2718
02:27:44,544 --> 02:27:46,754
so they can get their hands on the money.

2719
02:27:48,631 --> 02:27:51,384
Perhaps you ought to realize that Emmeline only wants

2720
02:27:51,717 --> 02:27:53,427
to be cared for.

2721
02:27:53,761 --> 02:27:55,388
Well.

2722
02:27:55,721 --> 02:27:57,481
If you have any compassion left in your soul,

2723
02:27:57,723 --> 02:27:59,517
you might spend it on her.

2724
02:28:00,643 --> 02:28:03,521
Children should be seen and not heard.

2725
02:28:11,237 --> 02:28:16,450
You seem to be very broad-minded in your opinions Miss Shirley.

2726
02:28:17,118 --> 02:28:18,661
That's the nicest compliment anyone's

2727
02:28:18,995 --> 02:28:20,872
ever paid me Mrs. Harris.

2728
02:28:30,548 --> 02:28:33,509
Pardon me young man, | was wondering if you would allow my

2729
02:28:34,010 --> 02:28:37,471
girls and me the pleasure of a hayride to town in your wagon.

2730
02:28:37,805 --> 02:28:40,558
It would be so exciting, but | promise you...

2731
02:28:56,699 --> 02:29:00,453
Mama, Mama!

2732
02:29:01,495 --> 02:29:03,039
You'll simply have to go.

2733
02:29:03,456 --> 02:29:05,374
Good-bye.

2734
02:29:14,634 --> 02:29:17,637
Mama, Mama.

2735
02:29:18,346 --> 02:29:19,555
What's happened?

2736
02:29:19,889 --> 02:29:22,600
Mama are you alright?

2737
02:29:23,017 --> 02:29:24,017
You're wearing a hat.

2738
02:29:24,143 --> 02:29:26,121
Mama | can't remember the last time you wore a hat.

2739
02:29:26,145 --> 02:29:27,647
Pauline will you calm yourself.

2740
02:29:28,022 --> 02:29:29,022
You sound hysterical.

2741
02:29:29,357 --> 02:29:31,943
You've seen me wear a hat often enough girl.

2742
02:29:32,360 --> 02:29:35,071
Miss Shirley suggested an Al Fresco lunch

2743
02:29:35,780 --> 02:29:37,949
it was most enjoyable.

2744
02:29:39,825 --> 02:29:41,744
I've been so anxious about you mama.

2745
02:29:43,663 --> 02:29:45,623
| was worried sick the entire party.

2746
02:29:45,957 --> 02:29:48,709
Will you stop fluttering girl!

2747
02:29:49,001 --> 02:29:50,628
You fidget me.

2748
02:29:50,962 --> 02:29:52,940
Pauline, did you have a good time at your wedding party?

2749
02:29:52,964 --> 02:29:55,633
Oh my yes.

2750
02:29:55,967 --> 02:29:58,636
Oh, Louise sent you her bouquet Mama.

2751
02:29:58,970 --> 02:30:00,596
The flowers were wonderful.

2752
02:30:00,888 --> 02:30:02,598
The parlour was a bower...

2753
02:30:02,932 --> 02:30:04,308
Like a funeral | suppose...

2754
02:30:04,767 --> 02:30:07,645
And the minister married Cousin Louise and Maurice over again.

2755
02:30:07,979 --> 02:30:09,647
Sacrilegious...

2756
02:30:09,981 --> 02:30:11,607
And Molly and Emily send their love.

2757
02:30:11,941 --> 02:30:13,651
Oh and Emily has the most delicious baby.

2758
02:30:13,985 --> 02:30:15,705
You speak as though it was something to eat.

2759
02:30:15,987 --> 02:30:18,656
Babies are common enough.

2760
02:30:18,990 --> 02:30:20,658
Babies are never Common.

2761
02:30:20,992 --> 02:30:22,660
Each one is a miracle.

2762
02:30:22,994 --> 02:30:23,994
Well | had two of them.

2763
02:30:24,245 --> 02:30:27,665
| didn't see much that was miraculous about either of them.

2764
02:30:27,999 --> 02:30:30,167
Mama you're so bright and cheerful today.

2765
02:30:30,710 --> 02:30:32,628
However did you two get along Miss Shirley?

2766
02:30:32,920 --> 02:30:34,880
| let her have her head and we got on well enough.

2767
02:30:35,047 --> 02:30:38,718
| don't care what the Pringles say...

2768
02:30:39,051 --> 02:30:42,179
| think you're quite good looking.

2769
02:30:42,680 --> 02:30:43,848
Thank you.

2770
02:30:48,394 --> 02:30:49,394
Oh good grief!

2771
02:30:52,356 --> 02:30:53,356
Well, well.

2772
02:30:53,524 --> 02:30:55,284
Little Bo Peep has lost her sheep and doesn't

2773
02:30:55,526 --> 02:30:56,526
know where to find them.

2774
02:30:59,405 --> 02:31:01,198
Good day Miss Kerr.

2775
02:31:01,532 --> 02:31:03,701
After this | shall be Surprised at nothing.

2776
02:31:04,827 --> 02:31:06,513
Leave them alone and they'll come home bringing

2777
02:31:06,537 --> 02:31:09,331
their tails behind them.

2778
02:31:34,857 --> 02:31:37,818
Get those sheep and that wagon out of here!

2779
02:31:38,444 --> 02:31:39,862
Papa!

2780
02:31:44,533 --> 02:31:49,080
Emmeline you were told to stop wearing those ridiculous

2781
02:31:49,455 --> 02:31:51,040
spectacles outside.

2782
02:31:51,373 --> 02:31:54,043
Your eyesight will never improve if you constantly wear them.

2783
02:31:54,376 --> 02:31:55,376
Yes Papa.

2784
02:31:55,628 --> 02:31:57,355
But Miss Shirley gave me these new ones and...

2785
02:31:57,379 --> 02:31:59,048
Go inside.

2786
02:31:59,381 --> 02:32:00,591
| mean immediately.

2787
02:32:00,883 --> 02:32:03,135
But...

2788
02:32:05,054 --> 02:32:06,054
Hurry up.

2789
02:32:09,642 --> 02:32:12,561
Young man whose fault is this?

2790
02:32:13,646 --> 02:32:15,564
Is this your wagon?

2791
02:32:21,946 --> 02:32:22,946
Thank you.

2792
02:32:23,114 --> 02:32:24,740
We had a marvellous time.

2793
02:32:25,032 --> 02:32:25,967
Miss Shirley...

2794
02:32:25,991 --> 02:32:27,052
May | have a word with you?

2795
02:32:27,076 --> 02:32:28,053
You run along, Miss Kerr.

2796
02:32:28,077 --> 02:32:29,077
Il catch up.

2797
02:32:30,621 --> 02:32:31,747
Yes, Sir.

2798
02:32:32,081 --> 02:32:36,877
It seems that each time we meet catastrophe lies in my way.

2799
02:32:37,169 --> 02:32:39,964
Well then perhaps you ought to get out of the way.

2800
02:32:41,048 --> 02:32:42,484
| get annoyed when people treat my instructions lightly,

2801
02:32:42,508 --> 02:32:43,843
Miss Shirley.

2802
02:32:44,176 --> 02:32:46,154
| gave explicit order that my daughter was to have no further

2803
02:32:46,178 --> 02:32:49,974
association with Kingsport Ladies College.

2804
02:32:54,603 --> 02:32:58,899
Would you mind telling me what the devil you're doing here?

2805
02:32:59,191 --> 02:33:01,110
We've been ona country picnic, sir.

2806
02:33:01,610 --> 02:33:02,862
Hosted by your mother.

2807
02:33:03,195 --> 02:33:04,864
My mother?

2808
02:33:05,197 --> 02:33:07,077
She authorized taking out all of those carriages

2809
02:33:07,199 --> 02:33:09,869
and inviting all those girls?

2810
02:33:10,202 --> 02:33:11,179
NO SIV.

2811
02:33:11,203 --> 02:33:12,872
| did.

2812
02:33:13,205 --> 02:33:15,875
And as she had nothing better to think about than herself,

2813
02:33:16,208 --> 02:33:18,878
| felt it was high time someone tried to help her.

2814
02:33:19,211 --> 02:33:20,188
Then you really are as insane as

2815
02:33:20,212 --> 02:33:21,964
all the rumours I've heard about you.

2816
02:33:22,548 --> 02:33:23,883
What have you heard?

2817
02:33:24,216 --> 02:33:25,885
You wouldn't want to know.

2818
02:33:26,218 --> 02:33:27,970
Yes | would!

2819
02:33:29,096 --> 02:33:32,099
The Pringles have labeled you the madcap English professor.

2820
02:33:33,142 --> 02:33:35,895
Someone said you had written the most ridiculous story they had

2821
02:33:36,228 --> 02:33:38,981
ever read published by... uh... something or other.

2822
02:33:39,315 --> 02:33:40,983
Reliable Baking Powder Company?

2823
02:33:41,317 --> 02:33:43,444
And that you were the silliest, redheaded,

2824
02:33:43,944 --> 02:33:48,115
mouse of a schoolmistress they'd ever known.

2825
02:33:49,200 --> 02:33:51,118
Thanks to you, | was very nearly fired!

2826
02:33:52,995 --> 02:33:55,195
There's a logical explanation behind everything, but you

2827
02:33:55,331 --> 02:33:57,750
people really are the most narrow-minded, self-centred,

2828
02:33:58,209 --> 02:34:00,127
quarrelsome group | have ever encountered!

2829
02:34:00,878 --> 02:34:03,005
I'd like to poison your entire clan!

2830
02:34:03,339 --> 02:34:05,966
You can't stand to see anyone succeed other than yourselves.

2831
02:34:06,258 --> 02:34:08,320
Oh, I'm sure you're all gloating over who will fly the victory

2832
02:34:08,344 --> 02:34:10,012
banner at the end of this year!

2833
02:34:10,346 --> 02:34:12,066
Well, you have not got the better of me yet!

2834
02:34:12,348 --> 02:34:13,348
Whoa, whoa.

2835
02:34:13,515 --> 02:34:16,018
Come back here.

2836
02:34:16,352 --> 02:34:18,192
You're upset by what the Pringles think of you?

2837
02:34:18,354 --> 02:34:20,154
| don't care to discuss it, if you don't mind.

2838
02:34:20,356 --> 02:34:22,024
I'm sorry.

2839
02:34:22,358 --> 02:34:24,211
You're afraid the Pringle rumours might reinforce

2840
02:34:24,235 --> 02:34:26,028
my conclusions about you...

2841
02:34:26,362 --> 02:34:28,030
Your conclusions?

2842
02:34:28,364 --> 02:34:30,032
Don't flatter your self!

2843
02:34:30,366 --> 02:34:32,344
You might be interested in listening to what | actually

2844
02:34:32,368 --> 02:34:34,161
had to say in your defence!

2845
02:34:34,662 --> 02:34:36,348
You ought to look around and see if there's anyone

2846
02:34:36,372 --> 02:34:39,250
you would like to listen to better than yourself!

2847
02:34:46,131 --> 02:34:50,928
| took it upon myself to see that this was delivered to you.

2848
02:34:52,012 --> 02:34:54,556
I'm sure you're far too busy to forward a change of address

2849
02:34:55,057 --> 02:34:56,892
to your daughter.

2850
02:34:57,226 --> 02:34:59,204
If you weren't so self-absorbed, sir, you'd realize there's

2851
02:34:59,228 --> 02:35:01,063
a little girl who desperately loves you.

2852
02:35:02,106 --> 02:35:04,066
You can go.

2853
02:35:14,034 --> 02:35:15,035
