02:50:35,872 --> 02:50:37,624
The audience was so unexpectedly moved.

3110
02:50:37,957 --> 02:50:40,501
It is our opinion that this proficient group of young

3111
02:50:40,877 --> 02:50:44,631
actresses must establish a permanent dramatic society.

3112
02:50:44,964 --> 02:50:47,467
"The Kingsport Examiner eagerly awaits their next production."

3113
02:50:51,721 --> 02:50:54,265
And on that note of praise, | hope you all perform

3114
02:50:54,724 --> 02:50:57,727
as triumphantly on your term exam next Friday.

3115
02:50:58,686 --> 02:51:00,271
Class dismissed.

3116
02:51:02,357 --> 02:51:04,025
Emmeline!

3117
02:51:20,917 --> 02:51:27,465
I'd like to apologize... for the... inconvenience

3118
02:51:27,924 --> 02:51:30,301
that | caused you, Miss Shirley.

3119
02:51:30,927 --> 02:51:32,071
We're all glad to see that your health

3120
02:51:32,095 --> 02:51:34,722
has improved... so quickly.

3121
02:51:35,098 --> 02:51:36,724
Yes.

3122
02:51:37,100 --> 02:51:39,894
| think that the doctor was overly concerned.

3123
02:51:41,604 --> 02:51:48,820
| hope | may stay in the dramatic society - if you're

3124
02:51:49,195 --> 02:51:50,947
going to continue.

3125
02:51:51,406 --> 02:51:54,826
Oh. We couldn't do without you.

3126
02:51:55,201 --> 02:51:57,829
Oh, thank you, Miss Shirley!

3127
02:51:58,204 --> 02:52:00,373
Oh - my mother wants to know if you'd like to help

3128
02:52:00,665 --> 02:52:02,834
with the annual hospital bazaar.

3129
02:52:03,209 --> 02:52:04,186
If you have the time.

3130
02:52:04,210 --> 02:52:07,463
Tell your mother I'd be flattered!

3131
02:52:17,932 --> 02:52:18,932
Good afternoon girls.

3132
02:52:19,100 --> 02:52:20,601
Oh Anne.

3133
02:52:20,935 --> 02:52:21,935
Hello.

3134
02:52:22,603 --> 02:52:24,605
The Board was totally enthralled.

3135
02:52:24,939 --> 02:52:25,874
Better than that

3136
02:52:25,898 --> 02:52:27,501
they were absolutely floored when they received.

3137
02:52:27,525 --> 02:52:28,609
Captain Harris' cheque.

3138
02:52:28,943 --> 02:52:31,779
They want to renew your contract for five years!

3139
02:52:32,113 --> 02:52:33,781
Five years!

3140
02:52:34,115 --> 02:52:35,783
I'm not sure | could last that long.

3141
02:52:36,117 --> 02:52:38,178
Well, | think that you ought to write a book about it.

3142
02:52:38,202 --> 02:52:40,872
Oh Miss Brooke isn't it wonderful!

3143
02:52:41,205 --> 02:52:42,445
Authors are such kittle kattle.

3144
02:52:42,665 --> 02:52:46,878
| wouldn't trust your description of any of us.

3145
02:52:47,211 --> 02:52:49,881
Here, these came for you.

3146
02:52:50,214 --> 02:52:51,674
Thank you.

3147
02:52:54,052 --> 02:52:57,972
Oh!

3148
02:52:58,973 --> 02:52:59,973
Thank you again.

3149
02:53:00,183 --> 02:53:01,543
| would like to return the favour.

3150
02:53:02,226 --> 02:53:03,946
I'd be pleased to have you escort my family

3151
02:53:04,228 --> 02:53:07,899
for a short visit to Boston when | return in a month.

3152
02:53:08,649 --> 02:53:11,402
Sincerely, Morgan Harris.

3153
02:53:15,239 --> 02:53:19,160
Oh, they're beautiful!

3154
02:53:28,086 --> 02:53:32,006
Pauline Harris you don't know If you're coming or going girl.

3155
02:53:33,091 --> 02:53:36,010
Move that hatbox.

3156
02:53:37,095 --> 02:53:41,015
Not up there girl you'll brain me.

3157
02:53:41,349 --> 02:53:42,326
It's not safe up there either.

3158
02:53:42,350 --> 02:53:43,601
Put it back girl, put it back!

3159
02:53:44,185 --> 02:53:49,023
Lower the blind, it needs to be just about one inch lower.

3160
02:53:49,357 --> 02:53:52,026
Oh Pauline... Pauline.

3161
02:53:52,360 --> 02:53:56,030
Now you've done it!

3162
02:53:56,364 --> 02:53:58,449
All that light makes my headache worse.

3163
02:53:58,741 --> 02:53:59,741
I'm sorry Mama.

3164
02:54:03,204 --> 02:54:05,004
Well, you've got your colour back Mrs. Harris;

3165
02:54:05,206 --> 02:54:07,500
you must be feeling better.

3166
02:54:08,209 --> 02:54:13,047
Lam completely worn out with all the worry

3167
02:54:13,381 --> 02:54:14,549
and motion sickness.

3168
02:54:14,924 --> 02:54:16,244
My stomach is dropping out of me.

3169
02:54:16,426 --> 02:54:18,306
Why | ever listened to you and came on this trip

3170
02:54:18,636 --> 02:54:19,637
in the first place...

3171
02:54:20,138 --> 02:54:22,056
Now, now... we're almost there.

3172
02:54:22,390 --> 02:54:24,058
Perhaps you'd like some lunch Pauline.

3173
02:54:24,392 --> 02:54:26,060
We are not hungry.

3174
02:54:26,394 --> 02:54:29,063
Can they make a decent cup of tea on this contraption?

3175
02:54:29,397 --> 02:54:32,066
I'd rather drink mud than the tea that some people make.

3176
02:54:32,400 --> 02:54:33,400
Yes Mrs. Harris.

3177
02:54:33,609 --> 02:54:34,777
Il see what | can procure.

3178
02:54:35,194 --> 02:54:37,989
..and see that they wash the cup out properly.

3179
02:54:38,489 --> 02:54:41,868
| don't mean to be a trouble to anyone... but the way I'm feeling

3180
02:54:42,702 --> 02:54:45,163
| don't think I'll be here much longer.

3181
02:54:45,496 --> 02:54:48,624
Then perhaps you'll appreciate me.

3182
02:54:57,008 --> 02:54:58,509
Poor Aunt Pauline.

3183
02:54:59,051 --> 02:55:02,180
Oh well, grandmama will sleep for days once we get there.

3184
02:55:02,513 --> 02:55:04,193
| can hardly wait to see Papa's new house.

3185
02:55:04,515 --> 02:55:07,185
I've only ever heard of how wonderful it is.

3186
02:55:07,518 --> 02:55:11,105
I've a feeling we're all here on approval.

3187
02:55:11,481 --> 02:55:13,241
Papa thinks very highly of you, Miss Shirley.

3188
02:55:13,524 --> 02:55:15,693
He said so.

3189
02:55:20,364 --> 02:55:23,201
Hello, how is mother?

3190
02:55:23,534 --> 02:55:26,204
She allowed us to order her a cup of tea.

3191
02:55:26,537 --> 02:55:28,206
However, she Is throwing out complaints

3192
02:55:28,539 --> 02:55:30,208
at the speed of this train.

3193
02:55:30,541 --> 02:55:32,181
If we like your new house in Boston Papa,

3194
02:55:32,418 --> 02:55:33,920
can Miss Shirley and | stay with you?

3195
02:55:34,378 --> 02:55:35,522
Hmm, | don't know if Boston's large enough

3196
02:55:35,546 --> 02:55:37,924
for two sophisticated ladies.

3197
02:55:39,759 --> 02:55:42,136
Going from Avonlea to Kingsport was an adventure Captain.

3198
02:55:42,595 --> 02:55:44,472
| assure you this will be an epoch in my life.

3199
02:55:44,764 --> 02:55:47,558
Well, I'm sure you and Boston will make quite an impression

3200
02:55:47,850 --> 02:55:49,393
on each other.

3201
02:55:49,852 --> 02:55:52,730
If |can remember not to look as backward as | feel.

3202
02:56:08,871 --> 02:56:11,707
All this moving about

3203
02:56:12,041 --> 02:56:15,711
my neuritis is agony and nobody cares what | suffer.

3204
02:56:16,045 --> 02:56:17,171
Mother...

3205
02:56:17,505 --> 02:56:19,225
So this is what you've been wasting my money

3206
02:56:19,257 --> 02:56:20,591
on Morgan Harris.

3207
02:56:55,710 --> 02:56:58,629
| didn't invite you all the way to Boston to carry on like this!

3208
02:56:58,963 --> 02:57:00,548
It isn't fair, Morgan.

3209
02:57:00,881 --> 02:57:01,858
It simply isn't fair!

3210
02:57:01,882 --> 02:57:04,552
The child had got to come back and live with you!

3211
02:57:04,885 --> 02:57:06,512
| can't afford the expenses and | simply

3212
02:57:06,846 --> 02:57:08,556
can't stand the trouble!

3213
02:57:08,889 --> 02:57:10,867
Pauline has got quite enough to do - Oh, | don't mind mama.

3214
02:57:10,891 --> 02:57:12,560
Please don't contradict me!

3215
02:57:12,893 --> 02:57:14,562
Don't be so demanding!

3216
02:57:14,895 --> 02:57:16,039
She's back in school, besides | thought

3217
02:57:16,063 --> 02:57:18,399
you enjoyed having her with you!

3218
02:57:18,733 --> 02:57:22,570
Lam 79 years of age, my boy, and | can't be bothered

3219
02:57:22,903 --> 02:57:24,572
with the child.

3220
02:57:24,905 --> 02:57:27,450
You've got this enormous house!

3221
02:57:27,783 --> 02:57:29,863
It all comes out of your father's estate, doesn't it?

3222
02:57:30,077 --> 02:57:31,054
Huh?

3223
02:57:31,078 --> 02:57:33,873
| have every right to be 'demanding'!

3224
02:57:34,248 --> 02:57:37,001
Why don't you get married again?

3225
02:57:37,335 --> 02:57:38,961
| haven't the temperament for it.

3226
02:57:39,337 --> 02:57:41,005
| suppose no one would take you!

3227
02:57:41,339 --> 02:57:44,091
Mind your own business, mother!

3228
02:57:45,926 --> 02:57:49,055
Of course, | realize my opinions don't matter any longer.

3229
02:57:50,139 --> 02:57:51,766
| might just as well be dead.

3230
02:57:52,141 --> 02:57:53,809
Then you can have the rest of the money!

3231
02:57:54,143 --> 02:57:56,979
Please don't say that, mama - will say it!

3232
02:57:57,480 --> 02:58:00,775
You're two ungrateful children!

3233
02:58:01,150 --> 02:58:03,819
How many times have | sat up at night, nursing you?

3234
02:58:04,153 --> 02:58:05,130
When you were little?

3235
02:58:05,154 --> 02:58:07,865
Sometimes | thought you'd never live to see the dawn!

3236
02:58:08,824 --> 02:58:11,452
A mother's sacrifices are soon forgotten.

3237
02:58:11,786 --> 02:58:12,763
Mama.

3238
02:58:12,787 --> 02:58:13,787
Please come to bed.

3239
02:58:13,996 --> 02:58:14,973
It's just the strain of being.

3240
02:58:14,997 --> 02:58:17,875
Saints above, Pauline! Will you keep out of this?

3241
02:58:19,001 --> 02:58:20,252
Now listen to me, Morgan.

3242
02:58:20,586 --> 02:58:25,508
Lam not going to bed until you give me a decisive answer.

3243
02:58:26,008 --> 02:58:31,138
Face up to your responsibilities and behave like a man!

3244
02:58:31,472 --> 02:58:33,224
All right!

3245
02:58:37,978 --> 02:58:41,732
| shall look into making the arrangements as soon as | can.

3246
02:58:42,024 --> 02:58:43,001
Well.

3247
02:58:43,025 --> 02:58:46,028
That's better.

3248
02:58:46,529 --> 02:58:48,906
Goodnight?

3249
02:59:01,335 --> 02:59:02,837
Goodnight, Morgan.

3250
02:59:05,047 --> 02:59:08,759
You can't rely on that boy to stay in the same line for two

3251
02:59:09,051 --> 02:59:10,028
minutes together.

3252
02:59:10,052 --> 02:59:14,056
He'll toss that child back in my lap as sure as Sure can be.

3253
02:59:15,015 --> 02:59:18,936
And what do you think of my son's lack of responsibility?

3254
02:59:20,020 --> 02:59:21,020
| quite agree!

3255
02:59:21,063 --> 02:59:22,940
Goodnight, Miss Shirley!

3256
02:59:31,615 --> 02:59:33,534
Please... don't get up.

3257
02:59:34,618 --> 02:59:37,913
| just wanted to say what a lovely evening this has been.

3258
02:59:38,497 --> 02:59:40,737
And thank you for giving me such a wonderful opportunity.

3259
02:59:41,625 --> 02:59:43,544
| apologize for mother's behaviour.

3260
02:59:43,919 --> 02:59:46,547
In her condition, sarcasm is her one relief.

3261
02:59:47,631 --> 02:59:48,966
It's her Pringle nature

3262
02:59:49,633 --> 02:59:50,633
| suppose.

3263
02:59:52,136 --> 02:59:53,780
I'm surprised you've put up with all this Kingsport nonsense

3264
02:59:53,804 --> 02:59:55,556
as well as you have.

3265
02:59:57,641 --> 03:00:00,478
Well, it has been a challenge...

3266
03:00:00,811 --> 03:00:02,563
As well asa very good experience.

3267
03:00:03,647 --> 03:00:05,900
Oh, | desperately miss my Green Gables though.

3268
03:00:07,651 --> 03:00:09,737
Watching the home lights flicker across the pond

3269
03:00:10,196 --> 03:00:14,950
at night... Marilla waiting for me on the verandah.

3270
03:00:18,662 --> 03:00:20,581
Probably sounds very foolish to you.

3271
03:00:21,665 --> 03:00:24,502
Can't escape your wholesome Island upbringing...

3272
03:00:26,086 --> 03:00:30,007
It must feel very empty living in this vast house all alone.

3273
03:00:32,051 --> 03:00:34,011
Well, it's an investment really.

3274
03:00:35,179 --> 03:00:37,807
I'm away so frequently.

3275
03:00:38,933 --> 03:00:40,976
What is it that keeps you away from Kingsport?

3276
03:00:41,310 --> 03:00:43,979
Keeping occupied with the all-consuming problems

3277
03:00:44,313 --> 03:00:45,981
of my business.

3278
03:00:46,315 --> 03:00:47,983
Running away...?

3279
03:00:49,693 --> 03:00:56,742
No. Perhaps holding out for a reason to return.

3280
03:00:57,201 --> 03:00:58,994
Well, | hope you've found one.

3281
03:01:02,248 --> 03:01:04,625
I'm very grateful to you for all your hospitality.

3282
03:01:05,000 --> 03:01:07,670
Well, I'm very grateful to you for the pleasure

3283
03:01:08,003 --> 03:01:09,797
of such high spirits.

3284
03:01:11,924 --> 03:01:12,924
Goodnight.

3285
03:01:13,050 --> 03:01:14,844
Goodnight Morgan Harris.

3286
03:01:16,178 --> 03:01:22,977
Anne Shirley, | hope we shall see you often

3287
03:01:23,310 --> 03:01:24,645
when | return to Kingsport.

3288
03:01:33,195 --> 03:01:34,395
Let's try a new one, shall we?

3289
03:01:34,780 --> 03:01:36,115
Yes!

3290
03:01:41,745 --> 03:01:43,465
Do you think this makes me look older, papa?

3291
03:01:43,664 --> 03:01:44,664
Oh, yes, Emmeline.

3292
03:01:45,040 --> 03:01:46,351
We can't make up our minds which of these hats

3293
03:01:46,375 --> 03:01:48,127
look more sophisticated!

3294
03:01:48,460 --> 03:01:49,879
Neither can l.

3295
03:01:50,170 --> 03:01:51,213
We'll take all of them.

3296
03:01:51,881 --> 03:01:53,674
Papa!

3297
03:01:54,216 --> 03:01:55,216
Here she is.

3298
03:01:55,426 --> 03:01:57,136
The great lady of the West Indies.

3299
03:01:57,469 --> 03:01:59,138
She's magnificent!

3300
03:01:59,471 --> 03:02:01,056
What does "Mistral" mean, papa?

3301
03:02:01,432 --> 03:02:03,142
It means a "rough, cold wind".

3302
03:02:03,475 --> 03:02:04,475
Oh no, Captain.

3303
03:02:04,852 --> 03:02:07,146
It should be Christened after a delicious, perfumed wind.

3304
03:02:07,479 --> 03:02:09,148
Like a zephyr.

3305
03:02:09,481 --> 03:02:12,693
Then I shall name the next one the Zephyr in your honour!

3306
03:02:35,132 --> 03:02:40,220
..and the excursion to Boston all seems like a dream somehow.

3307
03:02:41,180 --> 03:02:44,475
Emmeline, who has had sucha forsaken life up to now

3308
03:02:45,017 --> 03:02:49,063
has blossomed and | feel Captain Harris now recognizes

3309
03:02:49,688 --> 03:02:52,316
the treasure he didn't know he possessed.

3310
03:02:52,858 --> 03:02:57,988
Lam a little weary of living out of a trunk though

3311
03:02:58,280 --> 03:03:02,534
and | long to feel the summer loveliness of home.

3312
03:03:02,868 --> 03:03:04,536
| miss you both so very much.

3313
03:03:04,870 --> 03:03:05,955
With all my heart.

3314
03:03:06,246 --> 03:03:08,207
Anne.

3315
03:03:08,624 --> 03:03:12,044
She's plain worn out if you ask me Marilla.

3316
03:03:12,336 --> 03:03:15,130
I'm not surprised, the way girls roam the earth now

3317
03:03:15,422 --> 03:03:16,423
is something terrible.

3318
03:03:17,299 --> 03:03:20,970
It reminds me of Satan in the Book of Job going to and fro

3319
03:03:21,261 --> 03:03:22,261
and walking up and down.

3320
03:03:22,513 --> 03:03:25,766
| don't think the Lord ever intended it...

3321
03:03:26,100 --> 03:03:29,770
What is to be will be Rachel.

3322
03:03:30,229 --> 03:03:32,356
And what isn't to be sometimes happens.

3323
03:03:32,690 --> 03:03:35,359
Riches are all very well Marilla.

3324
03:03:35,693 --> 03:03:39,446
But if Anne prefers the handsome unknown to Avonlea.

3325
03:03:39,780 --> 03:03:41,448
Well, there's nothing more to be said.

3326
03:03:41,782 --> 03:03:44,576
It's in the hands of Providence.

3327
03:03:48,247 --> 03:03:50,082
| enjoyed your company in Boston.

3328
03:03:50,416 --> 03:03:52,816
| hope the term is continuing well in Kingsport and Emmeline.

3329
03:03:53,127 --> 03:03:55,087
Is caught up now in her studies.

3330
03:03:55,421 --> 03:03:56,398
Thank you again.

3331
03:03:56,422 --> 03:03:59,216
Sincerely, Morgan Harris.

3332
03:04:17,192 --> 03:04:19,028
Anne Shirley.

3333
03:04:19,361 --> 03:04:20,988
What in heck are you doing here?

3334
03:04:21,572 --> 03:04:24,116
Gil?

3335
03:04:24,616 --> 03:04:26,994
You're the very last person I'd ever expected to meet out

3336
03:04:27,286 --> 03:04:29,163
here on a day like this!

3337
03:04:32,207 --> 03:04:33,207
C'mon.

3338
03:04:34,209 --> 03:04:36,354
The Royal Academy of Physicians is convening here this weekend

3339
03:04:36,378 --> 03:04:37,355
and I'm here as a delegate.

3340
03:04:37,379 --> 03:04:38,589
You must be proud of yourself.

3341
03:04:38,922 --> 03:04:41,082
Not as proud as | was of you when | read that clipping.

3342
03:04:41,175 --> 03:04:43,218
Miss Stacey sent me about the success of your play.

3343
03:04:44,303 --> 03:04:45,929
That's sweet of you Gil.

3344
03:04:46,305 --> 03:04:48,140
It's so good to see you.

3345
03:04:48,474 --> 03:04:50,514
Well | was actually hoping we'd run into each other.

3346
03:04:51,310 --> 03:04:53,246
| wasn't sure whether you'd be happy to see me or not, sol.

3347
03:04:53,270 --> 03:04:54,270
Happy?

3348
03:04:54,480 --> 03:04:56,356
| can't begin to express my happiness!

3349
03:04:56,857 --> 03:04:58,150
Let me look at you.

3350
03:04:58,484 --> 03:04:59,461
Oh yes.

3351
03:04:59,485 --> 03:05:01,205
Do | look like a young medical student now?

3352
03:05:01,487 --> 03:05:02,464
Not a bit.

3353
03:05:02,488 --> 03:05:03,488
You can't fool me.

3354
03:05:04,073 --> 03:05:06,116
You are still the same incorrigible Gil.

3355
03:05:06,784 --> 03:05:08,118
Tell me all the Avonlea news.

3356
03:05:08,494 --> 03:05:09,471
Have you been back?

3357
03:05:09,495 --> 03:05:11,175
Uh, no, I've been spending most of my time

3358
03:05:11,497 --> 03:05:13,123
with the Stuarts in Halifax.

3359
03:05:13,499 --> 03:05:15,125
Dr. Stuart's a very prominent surgeon.

3360
03:05:15,501 --> 03:05:20,130
It's he who arranged for me to attend as his delegate.

3361
03:05:20,506 --> 03:05:21,191
You see...

3362
03:05:21,215 --> 03:05:23,217
Christine and | are engaged.

3363
03:05:24,426 --> 03:05:26,637
It's set for next summer.

3364
03:05:27,763 --> 03:05:30,224
I'm so happy for you Gil.

3365
03:05:31,225 --> 03:05:34,103
| guess that's why | wanted to see you so much; To apologize

3366
03:05:34,436 --> 03:05:37,106
for being such a fool last summer.

3367
03:05:38,273 --> 03:05:41,944
You know, | think | understand now what you meant.

3368
03:05:42,277 --> 03:05:47,032
| meant what | said too and | won't ever forget you.

3369
03:05:49,660 --> 03:05:52,371
You turned out as | always imagined you would.

3370
03:05:53,455 --> 03:05:56,333
Doesn't it seem like yesterday we were off to Queen's

3371
03:05:56,708 --> 03:05:59,586
and vying for those scholarships.

3372
03:06:00,087 --> 03:06:02,214
| suppose you've kept up your writing.

3373
03:06:02,506 --> 03:06:04,007
Not really...

3374
03:06:04,466 --> 03:06:07,177
I've been busy and well Publishers aren't interested

3375
03:06:07,469 --> 03:06:09,847
in those kinds of stories.

3376
03:06:10,347 --> 03:06:12,182
Well | wouldn't give up altogether.

3377
03:06:12,474 --> 03:06:14,394
You know | always thought you should write a book

3378
03:06:14,518 --> 03:06:15,518
about Avonlea.

3379
03:06:16,228 --> 03:06:18,388
Change the name, of course, or Rachel Lynde would think

3380
03:06:18,522 --> 03:06:20,274
she was the heroine.

3381
03:06:20,566 --> 03:06:24,236
Avonlea is the dearest place in the world, | don't think

3382
03:06:24,528 --> 03:06:27,364
it's an interesting enough setting for a story.

3383
03:06:28,115 --> 03:06:30,426
Well, | intend to take Christine back to the Island with me

3384
03:06:30,450 --> 03:06:32,244
and set up my practice there.

3385
03:06:32,536 --> 03:06:34,472
Dr. Stuart has a lot of pull in Halifax and would like us

3386
03:06:34,496 --> 03:06:39,293
to live there, but | don't want any handouts.

3387
03:06:39,585 --> 03:06:43,130
Besides, any other place just wouldn't seem like home to me.

3388
03:06:43,589 --> 03:06:45,757
No, of course.

3389
03:06:48,594 --> 03:06:50,554
The Board of Governors at the college just offered

3390
03:06:50,637 --> 03:06:52,598
me a five-year contract...

3391
03:06:53,265 --> 03:06:55,350
That's wonderful.

3392
03:06:55,642 --> 03:06:57,328
You've certainly won your way into the hearts

3393
03:06:57,352 --> 03:06:59,479
of this affluent old town.

3394
03:07:00,230 --> 03:07:01,940
You won't be lonely.

3395
03:07:02,274 --> 03:07:04,401
I'll survive.

3396
03:07:04,902 --> 03:07:06,945
Well | ought to go.

3397
03:07:07,279 --> 03:07:08,279
Train leaves at 5:30.

3398
03:07:08,488 --> 03:07:09,948
Aw, no. Really?

3399
03:07:10,282 --> 03:07:15,954
Oh... Uh | was going to uh mail this but...

3400
03:07:16,538 --> 03:07:18,332
A note just isn't the same.

3401
03:07:18,624 --> 03:07:19,624
Thanks Gil.

3402
03:07:21,168 --> 03:07:22,961
Good-bye Anne.

3403
03:07:23,295 --> 03:07:24,295
Good-bye Gil.

3404
03:07:26,048 --> 03:07:27,966
Don't forget me.

3405
03:07:57,204 --> 03:07:58,204
Gill.

3406
03:08:00,540 --> 03:08:02,000
Gill.

3407
03:08:05,212 --> 03:08:09,883
Thank you, Good-bye.

3408
03:08:10,676 --> 03:08:12,594
Good-bye Anne.

3409
03:09:22,956 --> 03:09:26,376
Miss Shirley would you help US arrange all these garlands

3410
03:09:26,710 --> 03:09:27,687
and bunting?

3411
03:09:27,711 --> 03:09:29,338
This is a hopeless mess!

3412
03:09:29,713 --> 03:09:30,953
What's the matter Mrs. Pringle?

3413
03:09:31,214 --> 03:09:32,692
Not one of these nitwits has as much artistic ability

3414
03:09:32,716 --> 03:09:36,345
you have in your baby finger.

3415
03:09:36,720 --> 03:09:41,350
Ladies I'm putting Miss Shirley in charge here.

3416
03:09:41,725 --> 03:09:44,478
Let me see.

3417
03:09:45,645 --> 03:09:47,814
| suggest you gather it up in a rosette like this

3418
03:09:48,148 --> 03:09:50,268
and then we'll hang them with the festoons afterwards.

3419
03:09:50,317 --> 03:09:52,861
We were all so impressed with your production

3420
03:09:53,195 --> 03:09:54,297
at the college Miss Shirley.

3421
03:09:54,321 --> 03:09:55,864
Thank you.

3422
03:09:56,198 --> 03:09:58,992
And to think how you transformed Morgan Harris' little girl.

3423
03:09:59,326 --> 03:10:01,536
He's hardly had anything to do with the poor child

3424
03:10:01,995 --> 03:10:02,995
since she was born.

3425
03:10:03,330 --> 03:10:05,707
Such a tragedy when his Adelaide died...

3426
03:10:06,166 --> 03:10:07,292
She was a rare beauty.

3427
03:10:07,793 --> 03:10:10,337
Old Mrs. Harris and mother Pringle are first cousins.

3428
03:10:10,837 --> 03:10:12,881
And | know how the Harrises have cut themselves off

3429
03:10:13,215 --> 03:10:15,008
from everybody.

3430
03:10:15,342 --> 03:10:18,011
It was Morgan's fault though, she ran away and left him.

3431
03:10:18,345 --> 03:10:19,971
Terrible reputation with the ladies.

3432
03:10:20,347 --> 03:10:23,433
They say Adelaide really died of a broken heart.

3433
03:10:23,892 --> 03:10:26,019
I'm sure that he's felt sO guilty all these years

3434
03:10:26,353 --> 03:10:28,688
that he can't stand the sight of the child.

3435
03:10:28,980 --> 03:10:32,109
More than likely it's the old lady he can't stand.

3436
03:10:35,070 --> 03:10:40,075
Well | know for a fact that he has been seeing Elvira Evans...

3437
03:10:40,450 --> 03:10:43,078
Standard Oil Fortune from Boston.

3438
03:10:43,453 --> 03:10:49,084
She has been staying for the last two weeks at Maplehurst

3439
03:10:49,459 --> 03:10:51,294
or so my sister-in-law tells me.

3440
03:10:51,711 --> 03:10:55,882
You've gotten to know Cousin Morgan haven't you Miss Shirley?

3441
03:10:56,174 --> 03:10:57,174
Yes.

3442
03:10:57,467 --> 03:10:59,136
We've met on several outings.

3443
03:10:59,469 --> 03:11:01,680
He's very charming.

3444
03:11:08,687 --> 03:11:10,967
We're going to give Miss Evans a tour of the old town this

3445
03:11:11,106 --> 03:11:12,274
afternoon, Emmeline.

3446
03:11:46,224 --> 03:11:49,060
"Dear Miss Shirley, please accept our congratulations

3447
03:11:49,394 --> 03:11:52,230
on your book entitled 'Avonlea Vignettes.

3448
03:11:52,814 --> 03:11:56,067
Enclosed is our cheque for two hundred and fifty dollars

3449
03:11:56,401 --> 03:12:00,155
"as advanced against Our royalties."

3450
03:12:02,866 --> 03:12:04,034
Anne!

3451
03:12:04,409 --> 03:12:06,036
Anne?

3452
03:12:06,411 --> 03:12:08,038
Oh, hello.

3453
03:12:08,413 --> 03:12:10,040
Anne, | was hoping I'd run in to you.

3454
03:12:10,415 --> 03:12:12,584
We've missed having you back at Maplehurst.

3455
03:12:13,084 --> 03:12:15,396
| can imagine it must be very difficult for you to get away

3456
03:12:15,420 --> 03:12:17,047
from your important guest.

3457
03:12:17,422 --> 03:12:19,007
Yes, it is.

3458
03:12:19,382 --> 03:12:19,901
But please.

3459
03:12:19,925 --> 03:12:22,093
Don't apologize. | understand.

3460
03:12:22,427 --> 03:12:24,054
Good day, Sir.

3461
03:12:24,429 --> 03:12:26,149
May | offer you a ride back to the college?

3462
03:12:26,723 --> 03:12:27,723
No, thank you.

3463
03:12:36,441 --> 03:12:39,110
What's nagging you, Miss Shirley?

3464
03:12:40,362 --> 03:12:42,507
You're behaving rather like a spinsterly old school marm,

3465
03:12:42,531 --> 03:12:44,157
don't you think?

3466
03:12:44,533 --> 03:12:46,201
Perhaps that's because | am one!

3467
03:12:46,535 --> 03:12:47,512
| say that with admiration!

3468
03:12:47,536 --> 03:12:48,912
That was a compliment.

3469
03:12:49,371 --> 03:12:51,140
Lam a great proponent of independent thinking.

3470
03:12:51,164 --> 03:12:53,392
Moreover, | have always held that early marriages are a sure

3471
03:12:53,416 --> 03:12:56,962
indication of second rate goods that had to be sold in a hurry.

3472
03:12:58,964 --> 03:13:00,173
Wouldn't you agree?

3473
03:13:00,549 --> 03:13:03,176
Well you can be sure | am of the first rate kind, Morgan Harris,

3474
03:13:03,552 --> 03:13:05,530
and | certainly have far greater ambitions than marriage.

3475
03:13:05,554 --> 03:13:08,306
All that you are insinuating is nagging me.

3476
03:13:08,682 --> 03:13:11,184
| about to have a short work of fiction published!

3477
03:13:11,560 --> 03:13:13,645
Lam afraid it has me completely occupied!

3478
03:13:14,187 --> 03:13:16,314
Well, let me offer my congratulations!

3479
03:13:17,190 --> 03:13:18,125
Good day!

3480
03:13:18,149 --> 03:13:21,861
Anne... Anne!

3481
03:13:22,153 --> 03:13:23,863
Lam sorry.

3482
03:13:24,155 --> 03:13:27,075
| ought not to have such a back handed invitation.

3483
03:13:27,534 --> 03:13:29,136
I've been meaning to ask mother to invite you back

3484
03:13:29,160 --> 03:13:30,870
to Maplehurst.

3485
03:13:31,162 --> 03:13:32,872
How gracious of you!

3486
03:13:33,164 --> 03:13:35,142
But my schedule is so jam packed, | am sure! Won't be

3487
03:13:35,166 --> 03:13:36,918
able to squeeze it in.

3488
03:13:37,210 --> 03:13:38,210
| take it you'll attend

3489
03:13:38,253 --> 03:13:40,171
the hospital benefit tomorrow evening?

3490
03:13:40,672 --> 03:13:41,965
Yes.

3491
03:13:42,257 --> 03:13:43,967
I'm working as a volunteer.

3492
03:13:44,259 --> 03:13:45,969
| shall look forward to seeing you there.

3493
03:13:46,469 --> 03:13:48,109
Would you do me the honour, Miss Shirley,

3494
03:13:48,388 --> 03:13:52,601
of reserving me waltz on your card.

3495
03:13:53,435 --> 03:13:54,435
Of course.

3496
03:13:55,103 --> 03:13:58,898
I'd be pleased to, Morgan Harris.

3497
03:13:59,190 --> 03:14:00,190
Thank you.

3498
03:14:00,525 --> 03:14:03,695
If | have a waltz space free!

3499
03:14:10,535 --> 03:14:14,247
Well, what do you think?

3500
03:14:14,581 --> 03:14:17,876
You look like a Gibson magazine cover!

3501
03:14:19,377 --> 03:14:22,339
Perhaps some romantic artist will fall for you

3502
03:14:22,714 --> 03:14:24,466
and ask to paint your picture...

3503
03:14:26,551 --> 03:14:27,551
Oh, miss Shirley!

3504
03:14:27,719 --> 03:14:30,805
'm gonna wear my hair just like that when | turn eighteen!

3505
03:14:31,306 --> 03:14:32,474
You darlings!

3506
03:14:32,891 --> 03:14:36,227
Imitation is the sincerest form of flattery.

3507
03:14:36,561 --> 03:14:38,480
Would you run along and see if my cab is here?

3508
03:14:38,813 --> 03:14:40,148
Thank you!

3509
03:14:49,658 --> 03:14:55,372
My, my... Going to London to visit the queen, are we?

3510
03:14:55,705 --> 03:14:57,791
Are you not capable of saying anything pleasant?

3511
03:14:58,166 --> 03:14:58,809
No.

3512
03:14:58,833 --> 03:15:00,585
| haven't your talent for pretending things.

3513
03:15:02,170 --> 03:15:04,964
You take my breath away with your compliments.

3514
03:15:05,674 --> 03:15:09,594
You always have some secret delight, don't you?

3515
03:15:10,679 --> 03:15:12,472
Don't deceive yourself!

3516
03:15:12,847 --> 03:15:14,474
You'll never be one of them!

3517
03:15:14,849 --> 03:15:17,477
Despite you flaunting your string of pearls and making

3518
03:15:17,852 --> 03:15:20,188
a spectacle of yourself.

3519
03:15:24,693 --> 03:15:27,529
Morgan Harris is aman of status and achievement.

3520
03:15:27,862 --> 03:15:32,242
And you, my dear, are nothing better than a teacher.

3521
03:15:32,784 --> 03:15:35,495
| don't know what you mean, but | honestly

3522
03:15:35,870 --> 03:15:37,622
feel sorry for you, Katherine.

3523
03:15:37,956 --> 03:15:40,625
You shut out every spark of happiness around you.

3524
03:15:40,959 --> 03:15:43,712
| will not be poisoned by your bitterness!

3525
03:16:13,825 --> 03:16:15,618
You are good luck Anne Shirley.

3526
03:16:15,994 --> 03:16:18,329
This is the largest number of tickets we've ever sold

3527
03:16:18,830 --> 03:16:19,830
for the hospital.

3528
03:16:19,998 --> 03:16:22,667
Well, | enjoy helping out any which way | can Mrs. Pringle.

3529
03:16:23,001 --> 03:16:25,670
Don't get stuck behind that table all night.

3530
03:16:26,004 --> 03:16:27,338
Be sure to get a dance.

3531
03:16:27,672 --> 03:16:28,672
| will.

3532
03:17:10,965 --> 03:17:13,802
You took the teacher's course at Queen's.

3533
03:17:14,135 --> 03:17:15,112
Shirley, isn't it?

3534
03:17:15,136 --> 03:17:16,113
Anne Shirley.

3535
03:17:16,137 --> 03:17:17,722
Yes.

3536
03:17:18,097 --> 03:17:19,097
Lewis Allen.

3537
03:17:19,265 --> 03:17:20,865
| remember you won the Avery scholarship

3538
03:17:21,142 --> 03:17:23,770
and Gilbert Blythe won the Gold Medal.

3539
03:17:24,145 --> 03:17:25,313
Yes that's right.

3540
03:17:25,730 --> 03:17:27,398
Pleased to know you.

3541
03:17:27,690 --> 03:17:28,775
What do you do now, Lewis?

3542
03:17:29,150 --> 03:17:30,870
I'm the principal of Richmond Public School.

3543
03:17:31,152 --> 03:17:33,822
Not the most adventurous place in the world, but uh I've done

3544
03:17:34,155 --> 03:17:38,993
alright for myself, compared to a lot of others from Queen's.

3545
03:17:40,078 --> 03:17:41,913
Do you dance as well as you boast?

3546
03:17:42,247 --> 03:17:43,373
Better.

3547
03:18:20,326 --> 03:18:22,954
Morgan Harris certainly upstaged the Pringles

3548
03:18:23,288 --> 03:18:24,914
with that Evans woman.

3549
03:18:25,290 --> 03:18:28,668
They say she's a perfect cat.

3550
03:18:29,127 --> 03:18:30,127
Worth millions though.

3551
03:18:30,295 --> 03:18:33,047
I've met her and believe me it will take all his gold

3552
03:18:33,381 --> 03:18:35,675
to gild a pill like her.

3553
03:18:36,092 --> 03:18:38,094
A match of adjoining bank accounts, to be sure.

3554
03:18:46,477 --> 03:18:47,729
Anne! Anne!

3555
03:18:48,271 --> 03:18:49,623
Good evening Sir; Or rather Goodnight.

3556
03:18:49,647 --> 03:18:51,316
Goodnight?

3557
03:18:51,649 --> 03:18:53,276
You promised me a waltz.

3558
03:18:53,610 --> 03:18:54,610
I'm sorry.

3559
03:18:54,652 --> 03:18:57,322
My card was full all evening.

3560
03:18:57,655 --> 03:18:59,365
You needn't feel obligated to patronize

3561
03:18:59,782 --> 03:19:01,326
the local schoolteacher.

3562
03:19:01,659 --> 03:19:03,579
I'm sure you've paid handsomely for your tickets.

3563
03:19:03,661 --> 03:19:05,330
Wait a moment, let me explain.

3564
03:19:05,663 --> 03:19:08,291
Please don't spoil the evening for your guest

3565
03:19:08,583 --> 03:19:10,376
by causing a scene.

3566
03:19:29,812 --> 03:19:30,812
Anne.

3567
03:19:31,105 --> 03:19:32,607
Where are you going?

3568
03:19:32,941 --> 03:19:35,276
I'm quite exhausted.

3569
03:19:35,568 --> 03:19:38,738
Please don't complicate matters by making excuses.

3570
03:19:40,823 --> 03:19:42,617
Elvira Evansisa business associate.

3571
03:19:42,951 --> 03:19:44,929
For the past year | have been liquidating the last of her

3572
03:19:44,953 --> 03:19:46,621
father's shipping estate.

3573
03:19:46,955 --> 03:19:49,624
Bringing her to Maplehurst was a gesture of hospitality.

3574
03:19:49,958 --> 03:19:52,627
The conclusion of a lengthy transaction.

3575
03:19:52,961 --> 03:19:55,630
| know when I'm being conveniently excluded.

3576
03:19:55,964 --> 03:19:56,941
It isn't that at all.

3577
03:19:56,965 --> 03:19:57,942
Be reasonable.

3578
03:19:57,966 --> 03:19:58,943
Why should I.

3579
03:19:58,967 --> 03:20:00,468
| have no ulterior motives.

3580
03:20:00,760 --> 03:20:02,480
You're acting as fickle-minded as a breeze.

3581
03:20:02,845 --> 03:20:03,845
We all go on about you.

3582
03:20:03,972 --> 03:20:04,949
Even Mother.

3583
03:20:04,973 --> 03:20:06,641
She absolutely adores you.

3584
03:20:06,975 --> 03:20:08,953
Under the circumstances how could | have invited you

3585
03:20:08,977 --> 03:20:09,954
this evening?

3586
03:20:09,978 --> 03:20:11,854
| certainly wasn't fishing for an invitation.

3587
03:20:12,438 --> 03:20:14,649
Perhaps it's my wholesome Island upbringing, but | have

3588
03:20:15,024 --> 03:20:17,652
no intention of becoming "fancy's fool"!

3589
03:20:17,986 --> 03:20:20,655
| would like you to come back to Maplehurst.

3590
03:20:20,989 --> 03:20:22,657
Indeed | don't know why.

3591
03:20:22,991 --> 03:20:24,009
As Emmeline's governess perhaps?

3592
03:20:24,033 --> 03:20:25,660
I'll save you the trouble of asking.

3593
03:20:25,994 --> 03:20:27,662
| won't lose you Anne Shirley.

3594
03:20:27,996 --> 03:20:28,889
Let go of me.

3595
03:20:28,913 --> 03:20:29,913
Please, | would... oh!

3596
03:20:31,082 --> 03:20:38,881
Morgan Harris, oh I'm awfully sorry, but you grabbed me.

3597
03:20:39,966 --> 03:20:42,885
| want to ask you to marry me.

3598
03:20:43,970 --> 03:20:45,888
What did you say?

3599
03:20:51,477 --> 03:20:53,604
I'm in love with you.

3600
03:20:53,980 --> 03:20:56,774
You really mean that don't you.

3601
03:20:57,108 --> 03:20:58,776
My life on it.

3602
03:20:59,110 --> 03:21:03,781
| only know | could never bear to lose you.

3603
03:21:04,115 --> 03:21:08,911
Would you do me the honour of giving me your hand in marriage?

3604
03:21:16,002 --> 03:21:19,797
Anne, what is it?

3605
03:21:20,131 --> 03:21:25,803
| do care a great deal for you and Emmeline.

3606
03:21:26,137 --> 03:21:28,765
But | can't.

3607
03:21:29,098 --> 03:21:30,098
What do you mean?

3608
03:21:30,516 --> 03:21:32,636
| mean that for five glorious seconds | really thought

3609
03:21:32,685 --> 03:21:35,271
perhaps | could marry you.

3610
03:21:35,646 --> 03:21:38,357
| used to dream of a moment like this.

3611
03:21:38,649 --> 03:21:46,365
Now, | can't describe it, |need to go home.

3612
03:21:46,657 --> 03:21:48,367
You could go back for summer holidays.

3613
03:21:48,659 --> 03:21:53,539
Rent one of those big old places on the Gulf.

3614
03:21:58,753 --> 03:22:00,588
Not the same thing

3615
03:22:00,922 --> 03:22:03,508
is it?

3616
03:22:04,342 --> 03:22:06,511
No.

3617
03:22:10,139 --> 03:22:11,933
Look at you.

3618
03:22:12,266 --> 03:22:13,946
You're out here without even your coat on!

3619
03:22:14,268 --> 03:22:15,937
You'll catch your death.

3620
03:22:16,270 --> 03:22:18,064
We should go back in.

3621
03:22:18,439 --> 03:22:24,946
| still have a waltz free.

3622
03:22:25,279 --> 03:22:26,864
Alright?

3623
03:22:29,158 --> 03:22:32,703
Let's give those old ladies something to gossip about.

3624
03:22:35,581 --> 03:22:37,583
Come in...

3625
03:22:40,503 --> 03:22:42,755
Why Mr. McGuinness, what is it?

3626
03:22:43,381 --> 03:22:46,050
You must come quickly to Maplehurst, Miss.

3627
03:22:46,384 --> 03:22:48,052
Everyone's worried.

3628
03:22:48,386 --> 03:22:51,639
Mrs. Harris has kept silent all week.

3629
03:22:51,931 --> 03:22:53,599
Silent?

3630
03:22:53,933 --> 03:22:56,727
Something must be dreadfully wrong.

3631
03:23:02,650 --> 03:23:05,611
She took a bad spell just after Papa left.

3632
03:23:05,903 --> 03:23:08,614
Now she won't eat or drink and poor Aunt Pauline is beside

3633
03:23:08,906 --> 03:23:12,994
herself to know what we should do.

3634
03:23:21,169 --> 03:23:25,006
Miss Shirley thank goodness you've come.

3635
03:23:25,339 --> 03:23:27,216
I'm afraid that she's slipping away,

3636
03:23:27,550 --> 03:23:31,095
and it's all my fault.

3637
03:23:31,429 --> 03:23:33,264
Isaac Kent wants me to... to... marry

3638
03:23:33,639 --> 03:23:36,559
him... practically.

3639
03:23:37,435 --> 03:23:39,729
He's asked me to join the Presbyterian Church

3640
03:23:40,104 --> 03:23:41,314
choir league.

3641
03:23:42,231 --> 03:23:46,110
Mama hates Isaac as much as she did fifteen years ago when she

3642
03:23:46,444 --> 03:23:50,114
set the bull terrier on him for coming around to see me.

3643
03:23:50,907 --> 03:23:53,159
| don't think she'll forgive me.

3644
03:23:54,118 --> 03:23:57,622
I'm so afraid she's going to die...

3645
03:24:01,918 --> 03:24:05,129
You must choose between them, Pauline.

3646
03:24:05,463 --> 03:24:08,132
Oh, | don't think | can live without him!

3647
03:24:08,466 --> 03:24:12,136
Don't be frightened now, you must accept!

3648
03:24:12,470 --> 03:24:15,723
Oh, Miss Shirley!

3649
03:24:17,642 --> 03:24:20,811
You've always been able to smooth things over with mama.

3650
03:24:21,229 --> 03:24:24,232
Please try to get her to forgive me?

3651
03:24:37,536 --> 03:24:41,457
Oh it's you is it?

3652
03:24:41,791 --> 03:24:44,460
Mrs. Harris please hear me through patiently...

3653
03:24:44,794 --> 03:24:48,464
I'm always patient... very patient.

3654
03:24:49,215 --> 03:24:53,469
| want you to know that Pauline is greatly troubled.

3655
03:24:54,178 --> 03:24:56,931
She is of the opinion that she should accept Isaac Kent's

3656
03:24:57,473 --> 03:24:59,767
hand in marriage.

3657
03:25:02,645 --> 03:25:05,481
| thought there was some foolishness between her

3658
03:25:05,815 --> 03:25:09,694
and that ridiculous fellow!

3659
03:25:10,194 --> 03:25:13,572
In your heart you must know it's the right thing to do.

3660
03:25:14,657 --> 03:25:17,326
The truth is, Pauline needs your forgiveness if she's

3661
03:25:17,785 --> 03:25:19,495
ever gonna be happy.

3662
03:25:20,037 --> 03:25:22,081
| advised her to be married.

3663
03:25:22,665 --> 03:25:24,667
And | beg of you to let her go.

3664
03:25:27,461 --> 03:25:32,925
If you've managed to get Pauline to accept that Isaac Kent

3665
03:25:33,509 --> 03:25:37,763
you've accomplished more than | thought was humanly possible.

3666
03:25:38,973 --> 03:25:44,020
At least | shan't have to climb down and tell him to take her.

3667
03:25:47,523 --> 03:25:50,443
"| withhold not my heart from any joy..."

3668
03:25:50,776 --> 03:25:52,695
That is Bible authority for you.

3669
03:25:54,363 --> 03:25:57,408
My dear, Man is born into trouble

3670
03:25:57,742 --> 03:26:00,202
as the sparks fly upwards...

3671
03:26:00,536 --> 03:26:04,290
Job 5 verse 6 Miss Shirley.

3672
03:26:09,170 --> 03:26:13,090
Pauline... come... here... girl!

3673
03:26:17,803 --> 03:26:21,640
No one can deny Margaret Pringle Harris' place as a cornerstone

3674
03:26:21,974 --> 03:26:24,643
of our community.

3675
03:26:24,977 --> 03:26:26,857
It is with great remorse that we turn her spirit

3676
03:26:26,979 --> 03:26:29,648
over to her master.

3677
03:26:29,982 --> 03:26:32,651
Though our hearts be troubled with this grave loss,

3678
03:26:32,985 --> 03:26:36,655
we must remind ourselves of the fleetingness of our own lives

3679
03:26:36,989 --> 03:26:40,659
and that some day we shall rejoice with Margaret forever

3680
03:26:40,951 --> 03:26:42,661
in the hereafter.

3681
03:26:42,953 --> 03:26:45,831
Amen.

3682
03:26:57,009 --> 03:26:58,009
Good-bye.

3683
03:26:58,886 --> 03:26:59,929
Thank you.

3684
03:27:00,221 --> 03:27:01,847
You're welcome.

3685
03:27:05,935 --> 03:27:07,686
We're going back to Boston, Miss Shirley.

3686
03:27:07,978 --> 03:27:09,688
Pauline has accepted Isaac Kent.

3687
03:27:09,980 --> 03:27:11,899
I've decided to sell Maplehurst.

3688
03:27:14,944 --> 03:27:16,987
How | shall miss you Em.

3689
03:27:18,072 --> 03:27:20,699
But we will see each other again soon.

3690
03:27:20,991 --> 03:27:26,705
And | promise you | won't ever forget you, just you mind that.

3691
03:27:26,997 --> 03:27:28,707
| will.

3692
03:27:28,999 --> 03:27:30,501
Good-bye Miss Shirley.

3693
03:27:33,963 --> 03:27:36,882
There's no one in the whole world like you.

3694
03:27:43,139 --> 03:27:47,810
Please accept my condolences Morgan.

3695
03:27:48,102 --> 03:27:49,812
Mother mentioned you before she went.

3696
03:27:50,104 --> 03:27:54,817
She was very keen on you.

3697
03:27:55,109 --> 03:27:58,320
She was never one to throw away a compliment.

3698
03:27:58,863 --> 03:28:02,825
That means a great deal to me.

3699
03:28:03,117 --> 03:28:06,829
Will you not reconsider?

3700
03:28:07,121 --> 03:28:11,834
I've come very close to reconsidering...

3701
03:28:12,126 --> 03:28:14,420
But it isn't any use Morgan.

3702
03:28:16,088 --> 03:28:17,840
I'll miss you, Anne.

3703
03:28:19,091 --> 03:28:22,845
| hope you rent that big old house on the Gulf someday,

3704
03:28:23,137 --> 03:28:26,015
'cause I'll miss you too.

3705
03:29:12,144 --> 03:29:15,189
| haven't had a chance to thank you Miss Brooke it's been such

3706
03:29:15,481 --> 03:29:16,481
a rewarding year.

3707
03:29:16,815 --> 03:29:19,527
Don't be ridiculous, please.

3708
03:29:22,196 --> 03:29:24,615
Where will you be spending your summer holidays?

3709
03:29:24,949 --> 03:29:25,949
Here in this fire-trap.

3710
03:29:26,033 --> 03:29:27,701
Where did you suppose?

3711
03:29:28,077 --> 03:29:29,828
Why stay if you don't like it?

3712
03:29:30,162 --> 03:29:31,830
Why... why?

3713
03:29:36,502 --> 03:29:38,212
Don't trouble yourself.

3714
03:29:38,671 --> 03:29:39,689
You've paid your lip service.

3715
03:29:39,713 --> 03:29:41,215
Now good-bye.

3716
03:29:41,632 --> 03:29:43,551
| shall see you next term.

3717
03:29:44,677 --> 03:29:46,470
| won't be coming back next term.

3718
03:29:46,804 --> 03:29:50,474
I've given my resignation to the board and Miss Stacey.

3719
03:29:51,642 --> 03:29:54,103
| came here to ask you if you'd like to spend your holidays

3720
03:29:54,395 --> 03:29:56,105
with me at Green Gables.

3721
03:29:56,397 --> 03:29:57,707
Unless you have somewhere else you're going.

3722
03:29:57,731 --> 03:30:00,818
An outburst of charity...

3723
03:30:01,402 --> 03:30:05,072
I'm hardly a candidate for that yet.

3724
03:30:05,406 --> 03:30:07,646
Katherine Brooke whether you know it or not what you want

3725
03:30:07,783 --> 03:30:09,660
iS a darn good spanking.

3726
03:30:10,411 --> 03:30:12,246
It must have relieved you to Say that.

3727
03:30:12,580 --> 03:30:13,557
It has.

3728
03:30:13,581 --> 03:30:18,127
And I've wanted to say it to you for a very long time.

3729
03:30:18,502 --> 03:30:20,462
But | have asked you to come because the very idea

3730
03:30:20,588 --> 03:30:23,257
of you spending the summer cooped up in here is indecent.

3731
03:30:23,591 --> 03:30:26,260
You asked me because you feel sorry for me.

3732
03:30:27,011 --> 03:30:28,679
| am sorry for you.

3733
03:30:29,013 --> 03:30:32,766
You shut out life and now life is shutting you out.

3734
03:30:33,851 --> 03:30:35,769
Now are you coming or not?

3735
03:30:36,854 --> 03:30:39,773
What would you say if | accepted?

3736
03:30:40,107 --> 03:30:42,776
I'd say that's the first faint glimmer of common sense

3737
03:30:43,110 --> 03:30:44,862
I've ever detected in you.

3738
03:30:55,331 --> 03:30:57,249
Alright | accept.

3739
03:30:57,750 --> 03:31:00,169
Now you can go through the motions of telling me how

3740
03:31:00,461 --> 03:31:04,256
delighted you are and how I'll have a wonderful time.

3741
03:31:04,798 --> 03:31:06,925
Lam delighted.

3742
03:31:07,259 --> 03:31:10,054
But as to a wonderful time that will depend entirely

3743
03:31:10,346 --> 03:31:13,265
on you Katherine.

3744
03:31:20,564 --> 03:31:23,025
The murder trials in this Boston paper my niece sent me

3745
03:31:23,359 --> 03:31:24,519
are real interesting Marilla.

3746
03:31:24,735 --> 03:31:26,195
Full of heathen, that place.

3747
03:31:26,528 --> 03:31:30,115
| hope Anne will never go there again.

3748
03:31:30,949 --> 03:31:33,619
Can you imagine that new minister going on about how he

3749
03:31:33,952 --> 03:31:36,312
doesn't believe that all the heathen will be eternally lost!

3750
03:31:36,955 --> 03:31:37,955
The idea!

3751
03:31:38,290 --> 03:31:40,751
If they won't be, all the money we've been sending to the.

3752
03:31:41,085 --> 03:31:43,754
Foreign Missions will be completely wasted, that's what!

3753
03:31:44,088 --> 03:31:45,756
| wouldn't fret if | were you Rachel.

3754
03:31:46,090 --> 03:31:48,759
Goodness knows the world is full of beggars and it's a pretty

3755
03:31:49,093 --> 03:31:55,182
pass if we can't help a fellow being in need, Christian or not.

3756
03:32:01,480 --> 03:32:03,315
Marilla Cuthbert!

3757
03:32:03,607 --> 03:32:05,627
Don't you be buying any junk from those peddlers just

3758
03:32:05,651 --> 03:32:07,403
to satisfy your conscience.

3759
03:32:08,654 --> 03:32:11,782
Oh it's an ill wind that blows no good.

3760
03:32:12,533 --> 03:32:14,410
Come back here you'll kill yourself running.

3761
03:32:22,501 --> 03:32:24,336
Oh, Marilla!

3762
03:32:24,670 --> 03:32:25,647
Anne Shirley!

3763
03:32:25,671 --> 03:32:27,256
I'm home Marilla.

3764
03:32:27,548 --> 03:32:28,548
I'm home to stay.

3765
03:32:28,674 --> 03:32:29,674
Oh you blessed child!

3766
03:32:29,758 --> 03:32:31,343
How I've missed you.

3767
03:32:31,677 --> 03:32:33,303
We were looking for you tomorrow.

3768
03:32:33,595 --> 03:32:34,656
How did you get from Bright River?

3769
03:32:34,680 --> 03:32:36,348
| walked, dearest of Marillas.

3770
03:32:36,682 --> 03:32:38,434
We left our luggage at the station.

3771
03:32:38,767 --> 03:32:40,745
| got homesick all at once and | wanted to show Katherine

3772
03:32:40,769 --> 03:32:42,438
all my old haunts.

3773
03:32:43,397 --> 03:32:44,648
Welcome to Green Gables.

3774
03:32:45,357 --> 03:32:48,318
Thank you for having me Miss Cuthbert.

3775
03:32:49,570 --> 03:32:51,155
Aren't these blossoms fragrant?

3776
03:32:51,530 --> 03:32:52,465
Smell them Marilla

3777
03:32:52,489 --> 03:32:53,574
drink them in.

3778
03:32:53,991 --> 03:32:55,951
Now enough of that nonsense.

3779
03:32:56,452 --> 03:33:00,330
It's you | want to hear about, not drinking in blossoms.

3780
03:33:01,415 --> 03:33:04,376
You must be real tired, Katherine.

3781
03:33:04,752 --> 03:33:06,670
Come and have a cup of tea on the verandah.

3782
03:33:07,045 --> 03:33:09,423
Oh, let's go slowly Marilla.

3783
03:33:09,757 --> 03:33:12,384
I've dreamt of this moment all year.

3784
03:33:12,760 --> 03:33:14,511
| want to soak it all in.

3785
03:33:15,596 --> 03:33:18,348
Not if Rachel has anything to do with it, she'll want to spill

3786
03:33:18,640 --> 03:33:20,309
out all the news of Avonlea.

3787
03:33:20,684 --> 03:33:21,810
Oh Anne Shirley.

3788
03:33:22,186 --> 03:33:23,079
I've got so much to tell you!

3789
03:33:23,103 --> 03:33:24,980
There's so much going on in Avonlea.

3790
03:33:25,731 --> 03:33:28,525
Oh Rachel, | have so much to tell you!

3791
03:33:28,984 --> 03:33:31,195
It's so good to see you again!

3792
03:33:32,613 --> 03:33:34,448
Rachel, this is Katherine Brooke.

3793
03:33:34,740 --> 03:33:35,550
Rachel Lynde.

3794
03:33:35,574 --> 03:33:36,259
How do you do?

3795
03:33:36,283 --> 03:33:36,801
Pleased to meet you.

3796
03:33:36,825 --> 03:33:38,660
Come on in now...

3797
03:33:40,704 --> 03:33:43,540
Green Gables never changes.

3798
03:33:43,874 --> 03:33:48,504
That's the beautiful thing about coming home, don't you think?

3799
03:33:54,760 --> 03:33:56,678
Katherine?

3800
03:33:59,598 --> 03:34:00,849
What's wrong?

3801
03:34:02,768 --> 03:34:04,686
Can | help you?

3802
03:34:06,772 --> 03:34:08,440
You can't understand!

3803
03:34:09,775 --> 03:34:12,694
Everything's always been so easy for you.

3804
03:34:14,613 --> 03:34:15,614
I'm caught in a trap.

3805
03:34:15,948 --> 03:34:19,117
|- | don't' think I'm ever going to be able to get out!

3806
03:34:19,618 --> 03:34:21,703
You don't hate me any longer, do you?

3807
03:34:22,204 --> 03:34:24,122
Oh Anne.

3808
03:34:24,623 --> 03:34:28,627
Hate has got to be like a disease with me!

3809
03:34:28,961 --> 03:34:32,631
| can never lead a normal life, now.

3810
03:34:32,965 --> 03:34:35,634
Yes you can!

3811
03:34:35,968 --> 03:34:40,722
You'll be quite independent and free here!

3812
03:34:41,056 --> 03:34:46,019
When | was a little girl, | remember an old faded print

3813
03:34:46,353 --> 03:34:49,773
on my uncle's wall showing a string of camels

3814
03:34:50,107 --> 03:34:55,946
around a desert with a palm spring.

3815
03:34:56,280 --> 03:35:00,742
I've always wanted to travel and see that place.

3816
03:35:01,076 --> 03:35:07,499
To see the Taj Mahal, the pillars at Carnet!

3817
03:35:07,791 --> 03:35:10,335
| want to know, not just believe,

3818
03:35:10,627 --> 03:35:13,463
that the world is round.

3819
03:35:13,755 --> 03:35:17,301
| could never do it on a teacher's salary.

3820
03:35:17,593 --> 03:35:20,804
| shall have to go on forever, prating about discipline

3821
03:35:21,138 --> 03:35:24,433
and the inexhaustible resources of the dominion!

3822
03:35:26,143 --> 03:35:28,395
| always wanted to be your friend, Katherine

3823
03:35:28,687 --> 03:35:30,606
spelled with a "K".

3824
03:35:31,189 --> 03:35:36,486
Underneath all your prickles, you really are a kindred spirit!

3825
03:35:40,657 --> 03:35:43,285
Does life never frighten you with its bleakness,

3826
03:35:43,619 --> 03:35:45,329
Anne Shirley?

3827
03:35:48,665 --> 03:35:51,418
This is the first place that I've ever been to that feels

3828
03:35:51,710 --> 03:35:54,880
like a real... home.

3829
03:36:13,440 --> 03:36:14,900
Isn't he perfect?

3830
03:36:15,233 --> 03:36:17,903
He is the most perfect baby I've ever seen, Diana.

3831
03:36:18,236 --> 03:36:22,616
Every baby is the sweetest and the best.

3832
03:36:23,075 --> 03:36:25,994
Before he came! Wanted a girl so | could call her Anne.

3833
03:36:27,079 --> 03:36:29,915
But | wouldn't exchange baby Fred for a million girls.

3834
03:36:30,248 --> 03:36:32,918
If you had an Anne you'd feel the same about her.

3835
03:36:33,251 --> 03:36:35,671
Would you like to hold the baby Katherine?

3836
03:36:35,963 --> 03:36:39,091
No, no... I've never held a baby in my life.

3837
03:36:39,424 --> 03:36:41,009
Never held a baby!

3838
03:36:41,343 --> 03:36:43,095
Don't be silly.

3839
03:36:44,680 --> 03:36:47,099
I'm afraid of it going to pieces in my arms.

3840
03:36:50,185 --> 03:36:53,647
There you are, he's taken with you Katherine.

3841
03:36:59,778 --> 03:37:02,656
It feels so good to see you dear folk again.

3842
03:37:02,948 --> 03:37:05,492
| want to hear all the Avonlea news.

3843
03:37:05,784 --> 03:37:07,828
I've grown a whole inch since you left Anne.

3844
03:37:08,161 --> 03:37:11,540
And now that squirt Anthony Pye can't pick on me anymore.

3845
03:37:11,832 --> 03:37:13,552
Can't you think of any more interesting news

3846
03:37:13,792 --> 03:37:14,769
than that Minnie May!

3847
03:37:14,793 --> 03:37:18,714
Did you know that Gilbert Blythe was dying?

3848
03:37:19,464 --> 03:37:21,842
Minnie May hold your tongue!

3849
03:37:22,175 --> 03:37:24,636
What do you mean Diana?

3850
03:37:25,012 --> 03:37:26,847
We didn't mean to tell you so suddenly, Anne.

3851
03:37:27,180 --> 03:37:30,142
He took scarlet fever in mid-term.

3852
03:37:30,726 --> 03:37:33,562
He picked it up at the hospital in Halifax.

3853
03:37:33,854 --> 03:37:36,523
Terrible worn out with school | expect.

3854
03:37:36,815 --> 03:37:40,569
They got a trained nurse and everything's been done.

3855
03:38:26,740 --> 03:38:28,742
| picked this up at the Post Office.

3856
03:38:29,034 --> 03:38:31,661
It's addressed to you.

3857
03:38:32,287 --> 03:38:35,082
My... my book!

3858
03:38:35,415 --> 03:38:37,084
Well don't sit there shaking like a leaf!

3859
03:38:37,501 --> 03:38:38,919
Open it.

3860
03:38:40,837 --> 03:38:41,837
Oh Marilla.

3861
03:38:42,005 --> 03:38:43,757
This can't be real.

3862
03:38:44,841 --> 03:38:50,305
They accepted my manuscript last February with a $250 advance.

3863
03:38:50,847 --> 03:38:53,767
You're a great one for secrets.

3864
03:38:55,393 --> 03:38:58,688
It's not a classic ora romance or anything important.

3865
03:38:59,022 --> 03:39:01,733
Just a humorous book of stories | did about Avonlea

3866
03:39:02,067 --> 03:39:04,778
in my spare time last fall.

3867
03:39:06,863 --> 03:39:10,534
But it's mine, it's all mine.

3868
03:39:10,992 --> 03:39:15,789
"To Marilla and Matthew Cuthbert for their unfailing love and

3869
03:39:16,248 --> 03:39:20,710
support and for Gilbert who inspired me with the idea

3870
03:39:21,044 --> 03:39:23,588
in the first place.'.

3871
03:39:26,883 --> 03:39:28,718
You do beat all Anne.

3872
03:39:29,052 --> 03:39:31,805
Everyone'll think | put you up to it.

3873
03:39:32,973 --> 03:39:38,854
That's awful good of you; Especially considering Gilbert.

3874
03:39:40,689 --> 03:39:43,024
How sick is he really?

3875
03:39:44,901 --> 03:39:46,736
It's been a bad case from the start.

3876
03:39:47,070 --> 03:39:51,741
No one's heard anything the past week.

3877
03:39:52,075 --> 03:39:53,743
He has the Blythe constitution

3878
03:39:54,077 --> 03:39:59,958
in his favour though... if God wills it.

3879
03:40:02,127 --> 03:40:07,757
Marilla there's a Book of Revelations in everyone's life.

3880
03:40:08,091 --> 03:40:13,847
I've been so wrong.. If Gil were to

3881
03:40:14,139 --> 03:40:17,851
not knowing how | really care.

3882
03:40:19,269 --> 03:40:23,773
Oh, there there now.

3883
03:40:24,524 --> 03:40:27,068
What would | do without him?

3884
03:40:27,694 --> 03:40:32,908
We can't change what God determines.

3885
03:40:44,377 --> 03:40:48,965
Jerry Boote... Jerry Boote works for Mr. Blythe.

3886
03:40:49,591 --> 03:40:51,384
It must be a sign.

3887
03:40:53,845 --> 03:40:55,222
The worst would be more endurable

3888
03:40:55,597 --> 03:40:56,932
than not knowing at all.

3889
03:41:07,067 --> 03:41:09,986
Jerry! Jerry!

3890
03:41:12,405 --> 03:41:14,324
Jerry, wait!

3891
03:41:16,701 --> 03:41:20,538
Jerry do you know how Gilbert Blythe is doing?

3892
03:41:20,872 --> 03:41:22,624
| think, | think he's bad.

3893
03:41:22,916 --> 03:41:25,543
The Blythes are all hoping he's gonna get better.

3894
03:41:25,877 --> 03:41:26,877
| don't know.

3895
03:41:26,962 --> 03:41:28,546
The doctor figures maybe

3896
03:41:28,880 --> 03:41:30,560
he's gonna have a close shave yet, though.

3897
03:41:30,882 --> 03:41:33,551
Will you ask Mr. Blythe to give him this for me?

3898
03:41:33,885 --> 03:41:36,638
Come with me if you like and give it to him yourself.

3899
03:42:02,372 --> 03:42:04,207
Hello Gil.

3900
03:42:04,541 --> 03:42:07,085
It's me.

3901
03:42:07,419 --> 03:42:10,755
Anne.

3902
03:42:14,384 --> 03:42:16,344
I've come to ask you to go for one of our old-time

3903
03:42:16,553 --> 03:42:19,306
rambles in the woods.

3904
03:42:20,390 --> 03:42:24,227
Wish | could go.

3905
03:42:24,561 --> 03:42:26,271
| brought you my book.

3906
03:42:26,604 --> 03:42:29,232
I've been published Gil.

3907
03:42:29,566 --> 03:42:34,321
| wrote about Avonlea just as you said | should.

3908
03:42:35,405 --> 03:42:40,410
Without any "high faulting mumbo jumbo".

3909
03:42:41,828 --> 03:42:44,622
I've dedicated the inscription to Marilla

3910
03:42:44,956 --> 03:42:50,754
and to Matthew, and... to you.

3911
03:42:51,296 --> 03:42:53,882
| was planning on saving itas a wedding gift, and then

3912
03:42:54,257 --> 03:42:57,260
| just decided | couldn't wait.

3913
03:42:58,345 --> 03:43:04,267
Anne, there's not going to be any wedding, anymore.

3914
03:43:04,559 --> 03:43:07,479
You're gonna well again Gil. | know you will.

3915
03:43:08,063 --> 03:43:10,815
| called it off.

3916
03:43:11,775 --> 03:43:14,027
It wouldn't be fair to Christine.

3917
03:43:16,946 --> 03:43:18,448
Oh Gil...

3918
03:43:18,865 --> 03:43:21,618
There would never be anyone for me but you.

3919
03:43:42,639 --> 03:43:47,477
Oh, Anne, the summer's flown by so quickly.

3920
03:43:47,811 --> 03:43:50,480
A schoolteacher really is a Slave of time.

3921
03:43:50,814 --> 03:43:53,483
| don't know how I'm ever going to go back.

3922
03:43:53,817 --> 03:43:55,110
Don't be silly.

3923
03:43:55,652 --> 03:43:57,487
There's always another bend in the road.

3924
03:43:57,821 --> 03:43:58,821
Bend in the road.

3925
03:43:59,072 --> 03:44:00,490
There's no bend in my road.

3926
03:44:00,824 --> 03:44:06,204
| can see it stretching out in front of me to the skyline.

3927
03:44:06,496 --> 03:44:08,498
Katherine, just look at you.

3928
03:44:08,832 --> 03:44:10,500
You're rosy and healthy.

3929
03:44:10,834 --> 03:44:12,585
And you hair looks so attractive like that

3930
03:44:12,919 --> 03:44:15,505
instead of all pulled back.

3931
03:44:15,839 --> 03:44:18,508
Besides, | happen to know of two eligible young men

3932
03:44:18,842 --> 03:44:20,510
who've asked about you.

3933
03:44:20,844 --> 03:44:22,512
Really?

3934
03:44:22,846 --> 03:44:24,514
They're gonna be at the bonfire tonight.

3935
03:44:24,848 --> 03:44:29,352
Oh, | wouldn't know what to say to them.

3936
03:44:29,686 --> 03:44:31,146
Will you help me, Anne?

3937
03:44:31,646 --> 03:44:34,441
They'll just laugh at me and think I'm an old gooseberry.

3938
03:44:34,816 --> 03:44:37,610
You give yourself far too little credit.

3939
03:44:37,944 --> 03:44:39,696
| wish | had your confidence.

3940
03:44:42,157 --> 03:44:45,702
| can believe almost anything of this Green Gables of yours.

3941
03:44:47,787 --> 03:44:49,706
Well, mine's full.

3942
03:44:50,498 --> 03:44:51,498
I'll be along.

3943
03:44:51,624 --> 03:44:53,624
| want to make sure Marilla has three full bushels.

3944
03:45:08,183 --> 03:45:09,118
Hello Anne.

3945
03:45:09,142 --> 03:45:10,226
Hello Gil.

3946
03:45:10,602 --> 03:45:11,936
You're looking very robust.

3947
03:45:12,353 --> 03:45:15,273
Well, I... uh... 1 guess | just made up my mind

3948
03:45:15,773 --> 03:45:17,734
| wasn't going to let it lick me.

3949
03:45:19,194 --> 03:45:21,112
Care for a stroll down the lane.

3950
03:45:21,404 --> 03:45:23,724
| don't think there's going to be many more fine afternoons

3951
03:45:23,990 --> 03:45:25,658
like this left in the summer.

3952
03:45:25,992 --> 03:45:27,660
| wish | could, but...

3953
03:45:27,994 --> 03:45:30,663
Katherine and I, we're off to Alice Penhallow's bonfire

3954
03:45:30,997 --> 03:45:31,974
in an hour.

3955
03:45:31,998 --> 03:45:35,168
It's the first party I'm taking her to and she's very nervous.

3956
03:45:36,836 --> 03:45:39,255
How about | walk you across the pond.

3957
03:45:42,926 --> 03:45:45,762
| was really afraid for you Gil, until we heard you

3958
03:45:46,095 --> 03:45:47,472
were over the worst.

3959
03:45:48,014 --> 03:45:49,094
Well | was lucky | suppose.

3960
03:45:50,475 --> 03:45:51,851
I'm not quite my old self yet.

3961
03:45:52,936 --> 03:45:55,438
By the time term Starts I'll be in fine form.

3962
03:45:56,439 --> 03:45:58,233
I'm glad you came back when you did Anne.

3963
03:45:58,733 --> 03:45:59,733
It meant a lot to me.

3964
03:46:00,401 --> 03:46:01,444
| finally read your book.

3965
03:46:02,362 --> 03:46:04,072
It's a fine piece of work.

3966
03:46:04,364 --> 03:46:05,364
| knew you could do it.

3967
03:46:06,324 --> 03:46:08,868
The Publishers are already planning a second edition.

3968
03:46:11,162 --> 03:46:15,875
It was along lesson to learn, but you were right.

3969
03:46:16,960 --> 03:46:18,240
I'm not going back to Kingsport.

3970
03:46:18,461 --> 03:46:20,797
I'm gonna stay here at Green Gables and write.

3971
03:46:21,130 --> 03:46:23,299
Private girls' school was too rough on you, was it?

3972
03:46:23,967 --> 03:46:25,134
No.

3973
03:46:25,468 --> 03:46:29,013
It's just that | went looking for my ideals outside of myself.

3974
03:46:29,514 --> 03:46:31,492
I've discovered it's not what the world holds for you,

3975
03:46:31,516 --> 03:46:33,268
it's what you bring to it.

3976
03:46:36,354 --> 03:46:39,357
The dreams dearest to my heart are right here.

3977
03:46:41,401 --> 03:46:43,570
Well | hope you keep on dreaming.

3978
03:46:47,031 --> 03:46:51,286
It'll be three years before | finish medical school.

3979
03:46:51,619 --> 03:46:54,289
Even then there won't be any diamond sunbursts

3980
03:46:54,622 --> 03:46:56,291
or marble halls.

3981
03:46:57,208 --> 03:47:01,170
| don't want sunbursts or marble halls.

3982
03:47:02,463 --> 03:47:06,509
| just want you.

